also look like crap.

252
00:09:47,567 --> 00:09:49,033
- [Joel] It's the Ozark
Mountain Daredevils

253
00:09:49,033 --> 00:09:50,567
taking out the laundry.

254
00:09:50,567 --> 00:09:55,033
(Crow chuckles)
(vocalized trumpeting)

255
00:09:55,033 --> 00:09:56,633
- [Tom] Well, sorry you
all have to work so hard

256
00:09:56,633 --> 00:09:59,733
but I'm off to play a
couple of rounds of golf.

257
00:09:59,733 --> 00:10:01,133
- [Narrator] It was
on that first day

258
00:10:01,133 --> 00:10:02,833
of his return to Copasand--

259
00:10:02,833 --> 00:10:04,067
- [Tom] A shot rang out.

260
00:10:04,067 --> 00:10:05,400
- [Narrator] Sinbad
found himself charmed

261
00:10:05,400 --> 00:10:07,533
by a poor working
girl of the city.

262
00:10:07,533 --> 00:10:11,367
- Boi-oi-oi-oing!
- Condition red! Dive, dive!

263
00:10:11,367 --> 00:10:12,300
- [Sinbad] What are you called?

264
00:10:12,300 --> 00:10:13,733
- [Crow] They call me Mr. Tibbs.

265
00:10:13,733 --> 00:10:14,767
- Lubiria.

266
00:10:14,767 --> 00:10:16,767
- [Tom] What an annoying name.

267
00:10:16,767 --> 00:10:18,900
- Do you always stare at people?

268
00:10:18,900 --> 00:10:20,067
- Not always.

269
00:10:20,067 --> 00:10:22,567
- [Tom] Heh-heh-heh, well, uh.

270
00:10:23,500 --> 00:10:26,533
- Could I have a drink, please?

271
00:10:26,533 --> 00:10:27,733
- Yes.

272
00:10:27,733 --> 00:10:31,167
- [Crow] Yes, water
(breathes dramatically).

273
00:10:31,167 --> 00:10:32,000
- Let me pass.

274
00:10:32,000 --> 00:10:32,833
- Please.

275
00:10:34,633 --> 00:10:38,300
Won't I be able
to meet you again?

276
00:10:38,300 --> 00:10:39,500
- I doubt that.

277
00:10:39,500 --> 00:10:41,167
- [Tom] I'm retaining
a little water.

278
00:10:41,167 --> 00:10:42,967
It's kind of a yoke.

279
00:10:42,967 --> 00:10:45,000
- [Joel] Strike one, Sinbad.

280
00:10:45,000 --> 00:10:46,533
- Wait, how shall I find you?

281
00:10:46,533 --> 00:10:48,633
- [Crow] Just ask for the
girl with two buckets.

282
00:10:48,633 --> 00:10:49,467
Get it?

283
00:10:51,267 --> 00:10:54,500
- Should you want to, you will.

284
00:10:54,500 --> 00:10:57,233
- [Tom] In other
words, buzz off.

285
00:11:01,633 --> 00:11:03,033
- Lubiria.

286
00:11:03,033 --> 00:11:06,600
- [Joel] Look to this
day, graduate, hah.

287
00:11:06,600 --> 00:11:08,800
- [Narrator] But there
were still the poor people.

288
00:11:08,800 --> 00:11:12,133
Copasand was now a
weary, enslaved city,

289
00:11:12,133 --> 00:11:14,433
with bondage a common word.

290
00:11:14,433 --> 00:11:19,033
- [Tom] Next up on Slave
Search, funny Slave Carrot Top.

291
00:11:19,033 --> 00:11:20,500
- Without you--

292
00:11:20,500 --> 00:11:22,700
- [Joel] Heh, I'm
gonna do my chops.

293
00:11:22,700 --> 00:11:26,133
- I would speak to you,
who would stand to us,

294
00:11:26,133 --> 00:11:27,933
a bonded man, a drink.

295
00:11:27,933 --> 00:11:31,500
- Oh, go on, you'll
drunken up the heavens now.

296
00:11:31,500 --> 00:11:34,000
- [Tom] What, is
this Les Miserables?

297
00:11:34,000 --> 00:11:36,100
- It was hunger
that enslaved him.

298
00:11:36,100 --> 00:11:37,967
- Better than starving.

299
00:11:37,967 --> 00:11:39,767
- Let him look for happiness.

300
00:11:39,767 --> 00:11:42,533
- [Crow] Howard
Johnson is right.

301
00:11:43,667 --> 00:11:45,267
- Nothing is better
than starving.

302
00:11:45,267 --> 00:11:46,767
- What?
- What?

303
00:11:46,767 --> 00:11:50,333
- When you lose your freedom
for the sake of a full stomach.

304
00:11:50,333 --> 00:11:53,133
Listen to me, good people
of the city of Copasand--

305
00:11:53,133 --> 00:11:54,400
- [Joel] Consider Amway.

306
00:11:54,400 --> 00:11:56,600
- I have heard there's
a bird of happiness.

307
00:11:56,600 --> 00:11:57,900
We need only to go and find it.

308
00:11:57,900 --> 00:12:00,933
- In what land is this
bird supposedly flying?

309
00:12:00,933 --> 00:12:02,167
- [Joel] Did I tell you talk?

310
00:12:02,167 --> 00:12:04,367
- That I do not know
but this, old man,

311
00:12:04,367 --> 00:12:07,733
I will tell you, we
must look for it.

312
00:12:07,733 --> 00:12:09,867
Look for it until we find it.

313
00:12:09,867 --> 00:12:11,267
- [Crow] But I kid the poor.

314
00:12:11,267 --> 00:12:14,333
- I'll build a boat and
sail about the world.

315
00:12:14,333 --> 00:12:17,233
I'll sail and search
until I have found it.

316
00:12:17,233 --> 00:12:18,167
- And how will you find it?

317
00:12:18,167 --> 00:12:19,533
- [Tom] That's great, security.

318
00:12:19,533 --> 00:12:21,800
- You aren't even a merchant.

319
00:12:21,800 --> 00:12:22,733
- Here!

320
00:12:22,733 --> 00:12:25,067
My only fortune is my harp.

321
00:12:25,067 --> 00:12:26,467
- [Crow] Why do you
think that's funny?

322
00:12:26,467 --> 00:12:27,400
What's so funny?

323
00:12:27,400 --> 00:12:29,433
- Not enough to sail with.

324
00:12:29,433 --> 00:12:30,933
- What did you sell
your freedom for?

325
00:12:30,933 --> 00:12:32,167
- [Crow] Some Knicks tickets.

326
00:12:32,167 --> 00:12:34,333
- What would it
take to free you?

327
00:12:34,333 --> 00:12:35,900
- [Tom] This isn't open stage.

328
00:12:35,900 --> 00:12:37,733
- One piece of silver?

329
00:12:39,233 --> 00:12:41,567
Here, this is not so bad.

330
00:12:41,567 --> 00:12:43,533
Who will give me one
piece of silver for it?

331
00:12:43,533 --> 00:12:44,767
- Here, let me see!
- Scram.

332
00:12:44,767 --> 00:12:46,500
- I will buy it.
- I own the man.

333
00:12:46,500 --> 00:12:47,933
It is his right.

334
00:12:47,933 --> 00:12:50,933
- Here you are.
- Well, he made bail.

335
00:12:53,600 --> 00:12:55,367
- If you ever do
make your journey--

336
00:12:55,367 --> 00:12:56,333
- [Crow] Which I doubt.

337
00:12:56,333 --> 00:12:57,767
- You must not be selfish.

338
00:12:57,767 --> 00:13:01,200
Alone, your bird cannot
bring you happiness.

339
00:13:01,200 --> 00:13:04,200
- [Tom] Thanks,
I'll mull that over.

340
00:13:05,433 --> 00:13:07,200
- [Joel] What did
I get myself into?

341
00:13:07,200 --> 00:13:08,967
I just got into town.

342
00:13:10,767 --> 00:13:14,300
- [Crow] Ah, screw that,
I'm going for the bird.

343
00:13:14,300 --> 00:13:16,267
- [Narrator] One
man freed, but still

344
00:13:16,267 --> 00:13:19,133
there were thousands more.

345
00:13:19,133 --> 00:13:22,500
- [Joel] Guess I should've
brought more hats.

346
00:13:22,500 --> 00:13:24,167
- Sorry, Mr. Sinbad.

347
00:13:26,733 --> 00:13:30,900
- [Joel] Ah, great, I give up
my hat and now I'm the jerk.

348
00:13:32,100 --> 00:13:33,333
- [Narrator] And so
it came to pass that

349
00:13:33,333 --> 00:13:35,800
Sinbad's joyful
return to his home was

350
00:13:35,800 --> 00:13:38,767
marred by the poverty and
unhappiness of it's people.

351
00:13:38,767 --> 00:13:40,133
- [Tom] Dumb old poor people.

352
00:13:40,133 --> 00:13:42,067
- [Narrator] A
city without magic.

353
00:13:42,067 --> 00:13:45,200
Where the marvelous wonders
were long forgotten.

354
00:13:45,200 --> 00:13:48,567
Where the riches of others
enslaved the good people.

355
00:13:48,567 --> 00:13:52,733
- [Joel] So Sinbad went to
the Renaissance Festival!

356
00:13:56,900 --> 00:13:58,433
- [Tom] Wait just
a doggone minute!

357
00:13:58,433 --> 00:14:00,567
I'm still Sinbad, dammit!

358
00:14:01,567 --> 00:14:02,633
- [Crow] No, no, I'm Dutch.

359
00:14:02,633 --> 00:14:04,033
I don't want any furs.

360
00:14:04,033 --> 00:14:05,767
What am I doing here?

361
00:14:07,833 --> 00:14:09,933
- [Joel] Consider fur, brought
to you by the Fur Council.

362
00:14:09,933 --> 00:14:12,933
(celebratory music)

363
00:14:14,100 --> 00:14:16,900
That's an odd way
to go to communion.

364
00:14:18,000 --> 00:14:21,167
- [Tom] It's 27 Brides
for 27 Brothers.

365
00:14:22,867 --> 00:14:24,233
Yip yip yahoo!

366
00:14:24,233 --> 00:14:25,333
- [Crow] I used to
be able to walk,

367
00:14:25,333 --> 00:14:27,000
and now all I can do is this.

368
00:14:27,000 --> 00:14:30,133
- [Tom] My house shall not
be a house of hilarity.

369
00:14:30,133 --> 00:14:33,700
- [Joel] Help me, I
don't know how to stop!

370
00:14:35,567 --> 00:14:36,800
Been around the world
and I've never seen

371
00:14:36,800 --> 00:14:39,067
anything as stupid as this.

372
00:14:40,867 --> 00:14:42,700
- [Crow] When jesters drink.

373
00:14:42,700 --> 00:14:46,633
- [Joel] If you must
jest, don't drink.

374
00:14:46,633 --> 00:14:49,867
- [Tom] Hey, Paul Winter.
(Crow barks)

375
00:14:49,867 --> 00:14:54,033
- [Joel] It's not working!
(Tom yelps)

376
00:14:55,500 --> 00:14:57,333
- [Crow] Hey, now look,
everybody's gotta go.

377
00:14:57,333 --> 00:15:00,533
My parents are coming
home any minute.

378
00:15:01,900 --> 00:15:04,333
- [Joel] I'll get your check.

379
00:15:05,600 --> 00:15:06,800
- [Tom] (laughs)
Nothing's funnier

380
00:15:06,800 --> 00:15:09,033
than a jester on the floor.

381
00:15:12,000 --> 00:15:14,100
- [Crow] The two stages
of Jackie Cooper.

382
00:15:14,100 --> 00:15:15,033
Young, old.

383
00:15:15,967 --> 00:15:17,867
- I don't choose to beg.
- Nyeh.

384
00:15:17,867 --> 00:15:20,867
(retro '80's music)

385
00:15:24,033 --> 00:15:25,267
- Quiet, all of you!

386
00:15:25,267 --> 00:15:28,133
- [Crow] A table for
one is all I ask.

387
00:15:28,133 --> 00:15:29,533
- [Tom] The hell?

388
00:15:31,133 --> 00:15:32,800
- [Crow] Sinbad, the
kitchen is closed.

389
00:15:32,800 --> 00:15:34,500
- Who invited him?
- Who is this man?

390
00:15:34,500 --> 00:15:36,033
- [Crow] What a dope.

391
00:15:36,033 --> 00:15:37,567
- [Tom] Where'd
you get the zither?

392
00:15:37,567 --> 00:15:38,833
Wiener.

393
00:15:38,833 --> 00:15:40,100
- [Crow] Why don't
you go back there?

394
00:15:40,100 --> 00:15:41,300
- I'm a traveler of many lands.

395
00:15:41,300 --> 00:15:42,233
- [Joel] Big deal!

396
00:15:42,233 --> 00:15:44,600
- And stopping again right here.

397
00:15:44,600 --> 00:15:46,500
On the beautiful
shores of Copasand.

398
00:15:46,500 --> 00:15:47,800
- [Joel] Oh, it's
the great Sinbad,

399
00:15:47,800 --> 00:15:49,500
gracing us with his presence.

400
00:15:49,500 --> 00:15:51,967
- I'll handle this intruder.
- Watch this.

401
00:15:51,967 --> 00:15:55,300
- Just now, Sinbad, you
have incurred my anger.

402
00:15:55,300 --> 00:15:58,500
How dare you break in
here and disrupt my party.

403
00:15:58,500 --> 00:16:00,133
Uncouth wastrel.

404
00:16:00,133 --> 00:16:01,867
This noble city--
- This England.

405
00:16:01,867 --> 00:16:04,267
- Does not need
the likes of you.

406
00:16:04,267 --> 00:16:07,167
- Abdallah, if you
please to wait.

407
00:16:07,167 --> 00:16:09,233
If you will all just
wait for one minute.

408
00:16:09,233 --> 00:16:11,800
- [Joel] I have some
amazing discoveries.

409
00:16:11,800 --> 00:16:12,633
- I must insist.

410
00:16:12,633 --> 00:16:13,900
- [Joel] Sleep.

411
00:16:13,900 --> 00:16:16,233
- Believe me, I
come not to quarrel.

412
00:16:16,233 --> 00:16:19,633
On the contrary, but
with a proposition.

413
00:16:19,633 --> 00:16:23,500
- [Crow] You can increase
your income by $25,000.

414
00:16:23,500 --> 00:16:25,900
- [Tom] Sounds great.
Drop the chandelier on him.

415
00:16:25,900 --> 00:16:29,800
- An offer of value.
Well, tell us about it.

416
00:16:29,800 --> 00:16:31,333
What have you to offer us?

417
00:16:31,333 --> 00:16:33,400
- [Joel] Well, it's kinda
a work in progress really.

418
00:16:33,400 --> 00:16:36,067
- All night long I've
listened to you talking.

419
00:16:36,067 --> 00:16:38,567
Boasting and bragging
of your power,

420
00:16:38,567 --> 00:16:40,000
your wealth and your happiness.

421
00:16:40,000 --> 00:16:41,200
- Not me.
- Don't you know

422
00:16:41,200 --> 00:16:43,867
that when you die, that you die.

423
00:16:43,867 --> 00:16:46,067
These riches cannot
be taken with you.

424
00:16:46,067 --> 00:16:47,300
- [Crow] You have to sail the

425
00:16:47,300 --> 00:16:50,367
seven flipping seas to
find that out, Cha-Cha?

426
00:16:50,367 --> 00:16:53,067
- To bring happiness
to all Copasand.

427
00:16:53,067 --> 00:16:55,200
Find this happiness.

428
00:16:55,200 --> 00:16:57,200
Search all over the earth.

429
00:16:57,200 --> 00:16:59,600
Build up a fleet
of merchant ships.

430
00:16:59,600 --> 00:17:00,867
- [Tom] Do you wanna
take it outside, sir?

431
00:17:00,867 --> 00:17:03,733
- Goods to all
men, and establish

432
00:17:03,733 --> 00:17:06,633
forever the glory of Copasand.

433
00:17:06,633 --> 00:17:08,367
- [Merchant] He is mad!

434
00:17:08,367 --> 00:17:09,867
- He listened to a fool.

435
00:17:09,867 --> 00:17:13,267
A drifter trying to
teach the expert.

436
00:17:13,267 --> 00:17:16,533
- [Joel] Oh, Jerry, you always
come up with the right line.

437
00:17:16,533 --> 00:17:17,500
- [Crow] Oh, Jer.

438
00:17:17,500 --> 00:17:18,333
- Away with him!

439
00:17:18,333 --> 00:17:19,733
- Away with 'im.

440
00:17:19,733 --> 00:17:21,333
- Away with the troublemaker.

441
00:17:21,333 --> 00:17:22,500
- Get him out.

442
00:17:22,500 --> 00:17:25,600
- Abdallah, this
spattering must stop.

443
00:17:25,600 --> 00:17:27,167
- [Crow] Santa, be reasonable.

444
00:17:27,167 --> 00:17:29,133
- [Merchant] That Sinbad
speaks the truth then?

445
00:17:29,133 --> 00:17:31,500
- Yes.
- He promises us glory.

446
00:17:31,500 --> 00:17:33,700
And he has nothing
in his pockets.

447
00:17:33,700 --> 00:17:36,000
You believe him and
you are a fool, I say.

448
00:17:36,000 --> 00:17:37,500
- Why won't you listen?

449
00:17:37,500 --> 00:17:40,467
You're a bright man, but now
you don't act very bright.

450
00:17:40,467 --> 00:17:42,233
Listen to your elder.

451
00:17:42,233 --> 00:17:44,367
We must send the ships.

452
00:17:44,367 --> 00:17:46,533
(Crow hisses)
- Fajita coming through.

453
00:17:46,533 --> 00:17:48,000
Watch out, ohp sorry.

454
00:17:48,000 --> 00:17:49,467
- Perhaps Sinbad is right?

455
00:17:49,467 --> 00:17:50,433
- What if he is?

456
00:17:50,433 --> 00:17:51,667
Who cares if he should be?

457
00:17:51,667 --> 00:17:52,700
You mind your business.

458
00:17:52,700 --> 00:17:54,133
- Diat!
- What?

459
00:17:54,133 --> 00:17:57,133
- I don't have to stay here.
- You could do worse.

460
00:17:57,133 --> 00:17:59,600
- Now, vagabond,
you cause trouble.

461
00:17:59,600 --> 00:18:01,667
- Here, Sinbad, a drink
for the great traveler.

462
00:18:01,667 --> 00:18:02,967
He travels the seas
and saw the sights

463
00:18:02,967 --> 00:18:04,133
and still has nothing.

464
00:18:04,133 --> 00:18:05,800
- Get out, old fool.

465
00:18:05,800 --> 00:18:09,733
- [Tom] He just brought the
level of discourse way down.

466
00:18:09,733 --> 00:18:11,200
- If you don't listen to him,

467
00:18:11,200 --> 00:18:12,933
you're all worse
than hypocrites.

468
00:18:12,933 --> 00:18:14,167
- [Joel] You're hippopotamus's.

469
00:18:14,167 --> 00:18:16,867
- You disagree with
your Father's wisdom?

470
00:18:16,867 --> 00:18:19,033
You side with the wastrel?

471
00:18:20,200 --> 00:18:23,267
You have shamed us,
in front of everyone.

472
00:18:23,267 --> 00:18:25,733
- [Crow] You guys were
shameful before he got here.

473
00:18:25,733 --> 00:18:27,400
- I'll get ships
without your assis--

474
00:18:27,400 --> 00:18:28,667
- [Tom] I'm here to stop the

475
00:18:28,667 --> 00:18:29,900
chain of fear that's
plagued this family.

476
00:18:29,900 --> 00:18:31,767
- There are people who
are wiser than you.

477
00:18:31,767 --> 00:18:34,133
(laughter)

478
00:18:34,133 --> 00:18:36,033
- [Joel] I'm outta here, thanks.

479
00:18:36,033 --> 00:18:38,733
- Do better with it than you.

480
00:18:38,733 --> 00:18:41,133
The poor will wear
brocade clothes.

481
00:18:41,133 --> 00:18:43,700
They'll dance in the streets
and have gold to spend.

482
00:18:43,700 --> 00:18:45,100
- [Crow] Sinbad,
ladies and gentleman!

483
00:18:45,100 --> 00:18:47,533
He always leaves us laughing.

484
00:18:49,167 --> 00:18:50,167
What a jerk.

485
00:18:51,500 --> 00:18:52,867
- [Joel] Come on,
jesters, leave him alone.

486
00:18:52,867 --> 00:18:54,200
He's had enough.

487
00:18:55,500 --> 00:18:57,733
- [Tom] Oh, that went well.

488
00:18:59,000 --> 00:19:00,667
- Arrogant, smug merchants.

489
00:19:00,667 --> 00:19:03,833
- [Joel] Last time
I go to the rotary.

490
00:19:05,367 --> 00:19:06,600
- They will regret--

491
00:19:06,600 --> 00:19:09,733
- [Crow] Sinbad, the
resentful sailor.

492
00:19:09,733 --> 00:19:11,733
- Take me along
with you, Sinbad.

493
00:19:11,733 --> 00:19:12,933
- And who are you?

494
00:19:12,933 --> 00:19:14,133
- Hadibad is my name.

495
00:19:14,133 --> 00:19:15,933
Here I'm just a buffoon
that means nothing.

496
00:19:15,933 --> 00:19:17,667
But with you I could
do a man's work.

497
00:19:17,667 --> 00:19:18,933
Oh, please, take me with you.

498
00:19:18,933 --> 00:19:19,767
- [Tom] (chuckles) No.

499
00:19:19,767 --> 00:19:21,167
- Men work hard.

500
00:19:21,167 --> 00:19:22,667
- Oh, please, take
me with you, Sinbad.

501
00:19:22,667 --> 00:19:23,600
I will work well.

502
00:19:23,600 --> 00:19:24,533
I promise.

503
00:19:24,533 --> 00:19:25,433
- [Joel] What are you, nuts?

504
00:19:25,433 --> 00:19:26,333
No!
- Alright.

505
00:19:28,233 --> 00:19:30,033
You will be my first recruit.

506
00:19:30,033 --> 00:19:32,133
- [Tom] You're on
probation for six weeks.

507
00:19:32,133 --> 00:19:33,967
- Now let me go.

508
00:19:33,967 --> 00:19:36,233
I must plan for our future.

509
00:19:39,033 --> 00:19:43,533
- [Crow] Thank God he
didn't check my references.

510
00:19:43,533 --> 00:19:45,500
- [Narrator] The merchants
had made their decision.

511
00:19:45,500 --> 00:19:48,467
The condition of the people
was of no concern to them.

512
00:19:48,467 --> 00:19:53,200
♪ What condition
their condition is in.

513
00:19:53,200 --> 00:19:55,000
- [Crow] Now it's Siddartha.

514
00:19:55,000 --> 00:19:57,133
- [Tom] Was that a Howard
Hesseman reference?

515
00:19:57,133 --> 00:19:58,233
Rudolph Hess.

516
00:20:01,467 --> 00:20:04,133
♪ Where is love

517
00:20:07,700 --> 00:20:11,233
- [Crow] Hey, someone
took my fort down.

518
00:20:11,233 --> 00:20:13,733
Steve Martin's World of Birds.

519
00:20:18,033 --> 00:20:20,433
- [Joel] I'm a sprite.

520
00:20:20,433 --> 00:20:21,800
- [Narrator] Sinbad
wandered to the edge

521
00:20:21,800 --> 00:20:24,433
of the Enchanted Sea.
- And had a magic BM.

522
00:20:24,433 --> 00:20:26,600
- [Narrator] And began
to play his magical harp,

523
00:20:26,600 --> 00:20:30,367
in the hopes that his
troubles would be answered.

524
00:20:30,367 --> 00:20:32,800
(harp music)

525
00:20:36,933 --> 00:20:40,300
♪ Jim Dandy to the rescue

526
00:20:40,300 --> 00:20:42,000
♪ Jim

527
00:20:42,000 --> 00:20:45,900
♪ Alone my soul must always be

528
00:20:47,700 --> 00:20:49,033
- [Crow] Al Martino?

529
00:20:49,033 --> 00:20:52,867
♪ Is happiness beyond the sea

530
00:20:54,200 --> 00:20:56,700
(all howl like dogs)

531
00:20:56,700 --> 00:21:01,300
♪ Does it hide it's shining fair

532
00:21:01,300 --> 00:21:05,833
♪ In dark caverns waiting there

533
00:21:05,833 --> 00:21:07,333
- [Crow] Is that a
rhetorical question?

534
00:21:07,333 --> 00:21:11,100
♪ My heart laments
the years I've spent

535
00:21:11,100 --> 00:21:12,800
- [Joel] Sinbad, do you mind?

536
00:21:12,800 --> 00:21:15,433
♪ In search of happiness

537
00:21:15,433 --> 00:21:17,933
- [Tom] Boy, now she's
a tall drink of water.

538
00:21:17,933 --> 00:21:19,133
- [Joel] That's enough, you.

539
00:21:19,133 --> 00:21:22,800
♪ There's a place
where kindness dwells

540
00:21:22,800 --> 00:21:24,167
- [Crow] Is there a place
where you can shut up?

541
00:21:24,167 --> 00:21:27,933
♪ My heart would find it's rest

542
00:21:27,933 --> 00:21:30,833
- [Joel] How 'bout giving
it a rest now, Sinbad?

543
00:21:30,833 --> 00:21:34,967
♪ Happiness could you be love

544
00:21:34,967 --> 00:21:39,233
♪ Hidden in a maiden's eyes

545
00:21:39,233 --> 00:21:41,333
- [Tom] Sinbad Unplugged.

546
00:21:43,333 --> 00:21:45,667
- [Joel] If you find a
melody, Sinbad, hop on.

547
00:21:45,667 --> 00:21:49,500
♪ In my own heart lies.

548
00:21:49,500 --> 00:21:50,700
- [Crow] Next, thank you.

549
00:21:50,700 --> 00:21:53,800
♪ My love it must be
(Crow sighs)

550
00:21:53,800 --> 00:21:57,500
- [Joel] Sinbad, honey, I'm
begging you, please stop.

551
00:21:57,500 --> 00:21:59,000
Please.

552
00:21:59,000 --> 00:22:01,300
(Crow clears throat)

553
00:22:01,300 --> 00:22:05,300
♪ Each way I pray forevermore

554
00:22:05,300 --> 00:22:07,400
- [Tom] Um, Mr. Bad, the
apartment building next door

555
00:22:07,400 --> 00:22:10,000
has asked me to ask
you to shut up, please.

556
00:22:10,000 --> 00:22:12,500
♪ Moonlit sea

557
00:22:14,267 --> 00:22:17,767
- [Joel] Everybody,
just the goldfish now.

558
00:22:18,967 --> 00:22:20,633
- [Crow] Take it to
the bridge, Sinbad.

559
00:22:20,633 --> 00:22:22,533
Drop it in the water.

560
00:22:22,533 --> 00:22:24,533
(Joel exhales)

561
00:22:24,533 --> 00:22:26,333
- Sinbad.
- Don't do that.

562
00:22:26,333 --> 00:22:29,133
- Would you even look
at me waiting for you?

563
00:22:29,133 --> 00:22:32,400
- [Tom] Oh geez, did
you just see everything?

564
00:22:32,400 --> 00:22:34,300
- Where, Sinbad?

565
00:22:34,300 --> 00:22:37,167
- You are the fairest
woman I've ever seen.

566
00:22:37,167 --> 00:22:38,933
- You seem so gloomy.

567
00:22:38,933 --> 00:22:40,400
- [Crow] Here, have some Prozac.

568
00:22:40,400 --> 00:22:43,333
- Perhaps you long for someone
who does not care for you?

569
00:22:43,333 --> 00:22:44,833
- [Joel] Is she
a kabuki actress?

570
00:22:44,833 --> 00:22:47,733
- Your song pulled at the
very heart of Morgiana.

571
00:22:47,733 --> 00:22:48,867
I'm your friend.

572
00:22:48,867 --> 00:22:50,167
- [Tom] Oh, she's a groupie.

573
00:22:50,167 --> 00:22:53,033
- You must let me help you.

574
00:22:53,033 --> 00:22:55,100
I have the powers of my Father.

575
00:22:55,100 --> 00:22:57,767
- And where is your Father
that he has such powers?

576
00:22:57,767 --> 00:22:59,300
- Below the sea.

577
00:22:59,300 --> 00:23:01,100
Known to you as Neptune.

578
00:23:01,100 --> 00:23:02,800
- [Crow] Known to me as Fred.

579
00:23:02,800 --> 00:23:04,967
- If you were only to look
at his magical kingdom,

580
00:23:04,967 --> 00:23:08,667
you would see gold fin fishes
and mysteries beyond belief--

581
00:23:08,667 --> 00:23:11,000
- [Tom] Sure it's real to
you with your (mumbles).

582
00:23:11,000 --> 00:23:12,333
Yeah huh, mmhmm.

583
00:23:13,900 --> 00:23:16,133
- This land of worry
and come below--

584
00:23:16,133 --> 00:23:17,733
- [Joel] For a Carnival
Cruise vacation.

585
00:23:17,733 --> 00:23:21,100
- Most of this opportunity
and journey with me.

586
00:23:21,100 --> 00:23:22,933
- But I cannot.

587
00:23:22,933 --> 00:23:24,633
I must stay here
and keep my promise.

588
00:23:24,633 --> 00:23:26,133
- [Tom] I have a doctor's
appointment at the dentist.

589
00:23:26,133 --> 00:23:29,600
- I promised to bring the
Bird of Happiness to Copasand,

590
00:23:29,600 --> 00:23:32,100
and I must search
the Earth for it.

591
00:23:32,100 --> 00:23:34,767
And still my ships
cannot be launched.

592
00:23:34,767 --> 00:23:36,667
I have no money to
begin my search.

593
00:23:36,667 --> 00:23:37,500
- [Crow] No money?

594
00:23:37,500 --> 00:23:38,433
Well I gotta go.

595
00:23:38,433 --> 00:23:41,333
- You're honor bound I see.

596
00:23:41,333 --> 00:23:44,300
- [Joel] So what
are you looking at?

597
00:23:44,300 --> 00:23:47,100
- [Tom] Going back, sorry.

598
00:23:47,100 --> 00:23:49,300
- Bring a boat here.

599
00:23:49,300 --> 00:23:52,500
Begin to cast beneath
the waters below,

600
00:23:52,500 --> 00:23:54,267
and I shall be there,

601
00:23:57,367 --> 00:23:59,500
bringing you my golden fish.

602
00:23:59,500 --> 00:24:00,833
- [Joel] Oh wow.

603
00:24:02,733 --> 00:24:05,800
- [Tom] Right, I
love this lake, yes!

604
00:24:05,800 --> 00:24:07,800
- [Crow] She's a keeper.

605
00:24:08,800 --> 00:24:10,367
- Morning's coming.

606
00:24:11,400 --> 00:24:14,700
And we shall part now, Sinbad.

607
00:24:14,700 --> 00:24:16,133
Perchance I have--

608
00:24:16,133 --> 00:24:20,000
- [Joel] This is the
latest Taster's Choice ad.

609
00:24:20,000 --> 00:24:21,400
- Time will tell.

610
00:24:22,567 --> 00:24:27,133
(vocalized motor sound)
- Oh, by the way,

611
00:24:27,133 --> 00:24:31,300
I left $10,000 in the (garbles).

612
00:24:31,300 --> 00:24:33,300
- I will come, Morgiana.

613
00:24:34,600 --> 00:24:36,067
Riches from the sea.

614
00:24:36,067 --> 00:24:38,433
- [Crow] (chuckles
sarcastically) Riches.

615
00:24:38,433 --> 00:24:40,233
- You'll see, foolish merchants.

616
00:24:40,233 --> 00:24:42,167
All of you, you'll see.

617
00:24:42,167 --> 00:24:45,900
(doors sliding and shutting)

618
00:24:50,333 --> 00:24:51,967
(jump and cheer around)

619
00:24:51,967 --> 00:24:54,533
(circus music)

620
00:25:11,767 --> 00:25:14,700
(heavy breathing)

621
00:25:14,700 --> 00:25:15,933
- Oh boy.

622
00:25:15,933 --> 00:25:19,100
Heck, cavorting really
takes it out of ya.

623
00:25:19,100 --> 00:25:21,200
- Jestering is grueling.

624
00:25:21,200 --> 00:25:23,967
Movie made it look so easy.

625
00:25:23,967 --> 00:25:25,700
- Okay, you guys, now listen up.

626
00:25:25,700 --> 00:25:30,367
We got plans for the next
Junior Jester Meeting

627
00:25:30,367 --> 00:25:31,700
the first Tuesday of next month.

628
00:25:31,700 --> 00:25:33,500
Don't forget your dues.

629
00:25:33,500 --> 00:25:35,367
- I make a motion
that the next meeting,

630
00:25:35,367 --> 00:25:38,667
we do our cavorting
laying down on couches.

631
00:25:38,667 --> 00:25:40,233
- I can't make it next month.

632
00:25:40,233 --> 00:25:42,267
- Hey, but you're in charge
of the snack committee.

633
00:25:42,267 --> 00:25:43,300
- I'm sorry.

634
00:25:43,300 --> 00:25:44,533
There's really no reason to

635
00:25:44,533 --> 00:25:45,967
meet during the
summer, is there?

636
00:25:45,967 --> 00:25:47,400
- Maybe we should
dissolve the chapter.

637
00:25:47,400 --> 00:25:48,633
- Wait a second,
you guys, you can't

638
00:25:48,633 --> 00:25:50,667
dissolve the Junior
Jesters Club.

639
00:25:50,667 --> 00:25:53,900
Where else am I gonna
wear these shoes?

640
00:25:53,900 --> 00:25:56,833
- Okay, how 'bout we
meet June 4th, huh?

641
00:25:56,833 --> 00:26:01,233
- No, that's how we got Mr.
Be Natural practice that day.

642
00:26:01,233 --> 00:26:04,967
- Hey, we got commercials
sign, I think.

643
00:26:04,967 --> 00:26:07,067
- Crow, could you be
a dear and get that?

644
00:26:07,067 --> 00:26:08,467
We'll try to iron this out.

645
00:26:08,467 --> 00:26:09,967
We'll be back right back.

646
00:26:09,967 --> 00:26:11,433
(Crow forceful grunts)

647
00:26:11,433 --> 00:26:14,367
(retro 80's music)

648
00:26:17,833 --> 00:26:19,167
- [Joel] Oh boy.

649
00:26:20,367 --> 00:26:21,200
Oh boy.

650
00:26:22,200 --> 00:26:23,667
I'm drinking Jesterade.

651
00:26:23,667 --> 00:26:26,667
You know cavorting really makes
you lose your electrolytes.

652
00:26:26,667 --> 00:26:28,833
- [Narrator] And promises
you a happy life.

653
00:26:28,833 --> 00:26:32,500
Magic and riches for
the people of Copasand.

654
00:26:32,500 --> 00:26:33,767
- [Tom] Next on
The Price Is Right,

655
00:26:33,767 --> 00:26:36,200
Conray Stevies, come on down!

656
00:26:37,367 --> 00:26:38,167
- [Narrator] And
grumbled at having

657
00:26:38,167 --> 00:26:39,600
their rest disturbed.

658
00:26:39,600 --> 00:26:40,767
Who is this who rings the bell

659
00:26:40,767 --> 00:26:42,533
at this time of night,
they complained.

660
00:26:42,533 --> 00:26:44,233
What madness is this?

661
00:26:44,233 --> 00:26:47,000
- [Crow] What
fresh hell is this?

662
00:26:48,200 --> 00:26:50,067
- [Tom] Come on, let's
take back the nights.

663
00:26:50,067 --> 00:26:51,767
♪ Take back the night

664
00:26:51,767 --> 00:26:52,700
- [Narrator] Down
through marketplace

665
00:26:52,700 --> 00:26:54,300
and into the public square.

666
00:26:54,300 --> 00:26:56,933
- [Tom] Neil Diamond
tickets were on sale.

667
00:26:56,933 --> 00:26:57,767
- What is it?

668
00:26:57,767 --> 00:26:58,933
What could be happening?

669
00:26:58,933 --> 00:27:00,733
The whole city's
running like mad men.

670
00:27:00,733 --> 00:27:02,833
- [Crow] This is all the
earmarks of a run on the bank.

671
00:27:02,833 --> 00:27:04,767
(bell chimes)

672
00:27:04,767 --> 00:27:06,800
- [Tom] Antony!

673
00:27:06,800 --> 00:27:08,367
- [Crow] Here on the
north side of Persia,

674
00:27:08,367 --> 00:27:09,667
it's Prince Spaghetti Day.

675
00:27:09,667 --> 00:27:10,900
- [Tom] Antony!

676
00:27:12,000 --> 00:27:13,200
- What's the meaning of this?

677
00:27:13,200 --> 00:27:14,733
Who dares call the people?

678
00:27:14,733 --> 00:27:15,667
- I do!

679
00:27:15,667 --> 00:27:16,867
- [Joel] Oh yeah, everybody just

680
00:27:16,867 --> 00:27:18,533
stop your lives and pay
attention to Sinbad.

681
00:27:18,533 --> 00:27:20,433
- Yes, take him now.

682
00:27:20,433 --> 00:27:22,033
- [Tom] If I could just
do my opening joke.

683
00:27:22,033 --> 00:27:25,767
(clears throat) Women be
different from men, you see.

684
00:27:25,767 --> 00:27:27,700
- [Crow] (laughs)
That was not bad.

685
00:27:27,700 --> 00:27:29,533
- [Merchant] We do
not wish to hear you.

686
00:27:29,533 --> 00:27:30,367
- Let him speak.

687
00:27:30,367 --> 00:27:31,300
- [Crowd] Speak!

688
00:27:31,300 --> 00:27:33,633
- [Viewers] Give us Barabbas.

689
00:27:35,633 --> 00:27:36,900
- Hear me, free men.

690
00:27:36,900 --> 00:27:38,633
Hear me now as I speak to you.

691
00:27:38,633 --> 00:27:41,067
- [Crow] What if Jack Nicholson
worked at a Burger King?

692
00:27:41,067 --> 00:27:43,433
- [Joel] I think it
would go something.

693
00:27:43,433 --> 00:27:44,800
- [Tom] And I failed miserably.

694
00:27:44,800 --> 00:27:46,967
- I felt this goal
could be reached.

695
00:27:46,967 --> 00:27:50,567
But your illustrious merchants
would have none of it.

696
00:27:50,567 --> 00:27:52,700
They laughed all this off.

697
00:27:52,700 --> 00:27:54,767
I say to you people
that I will do this.

698
00:27:54,767 --> 00:27:58,033
- [Joel] Lose eight
pounds by Christmas.

699
00:27:58,033 --> 00:28:00,600
- And then I will
cast the silken net,

700
00:28:00,600 --> 00:28:04,667
and this I will do, catch
fishes with golden fins.

701
00:28:04,667 --> 00:28:05,900
- There is no such
fishes that can

702
00:28:05,900 --> 00:28:07,333
be in the ocean and
you very well know it.

703
00:28:07,333 --> 00:28:09,933
- This insolent dog is trying
to make fools of us all.

704
00:28:09,933 --> 00:28:12,900
- This idiot should be
thrown for his insolence.

705
00:28:12,900 --> 00:28:14,133
- [Crow] He's a Populist.

706
00:28:14,133 --> 00:28:16,467
He just can't stop him.

707
00:28:16,467 --> 00:28:18,067
- [Viewers] Burn the witch!

708
00:28:18,067 --> 00:28:19,300
Burn the witch!

709
00:28:21,367 --> 00:28:24,233
- And this I am sure
will satisfy you.

710
00:28:24,233 --> 00:28:26,433
I'll catch these
fish if I'm able,

711
00:28:26,433 --> 00:28:29,400
then you will give me the
keys to your warehouses.

712
00:28:29,400 --> 00:28:32,333
And should I fail, I freely
give you the head of Sinbad.

713
00:28:32,333 --> 00:28:33,767
- [Crow] And I'll insist
that you all spank me.

714
00:28:33,767 --> 00:28:35,833
- And now what do you say?
- Bite me!

715
00:28:35,833 --> 00:28:39,067
- You shall have his
head, I warned you.

716
00:28:39,067 --> 00:28:41,700
Whoever heard of
these golden fishes?

717
00:28:41,700 --> 00:28:43,933
- Well, what do you say?

718
00:28:43,933 --> 00:28:44,967
Is it agreed then?

719
00:28:44,967 --> 00:28:46,233
- [Viewers] No!

720
00:28:47,333 --> 00:28:49,367
- You have all
heard the agreement.

721
00:28:49,367 --> 00:28:51,867
Now we will see what
the morning will bring.

722
00:28:51,867 --> 00:28:52,967
- [Tom] Now, hang on.

723
00:28:52,967 --> 00:28:55,700
(crowd cheers)
- He has the entire day.

724
00:28:55,700 --> 00:28:59,067
Sinbad will cast his net
and catch his golden fish,

725
00:28:59,067 --> 00:29:02,900
as he promises, and if
he does not catch them,

726
00:29:02,900 --> 00:29:05,500
then his head will belong to us.

727
00:29:05,500 --> 00:29:06,500
So.
- Agreed.

728
00:29:07,667 --> 00:29:08,800
- [Joel] And I'm gone!

729
00:29:08,800 --> 00:29:10,333
Woap, maybe not.

730
00:29:10,333 --> 00:29:13,333
- [Crow] Jay Highland Brewing
Company, Lacrosse, Wisconsin.

731
00:29:13,333 --> 00:29:14,267
Over there.

732
00:29:14,267 --> 00:29:17,100
♪ Beyond the blue horiz--

733
00:29:17,100 --> 00:29:18,567
- Only the brave shall join me.

734
00:29:18,567 --> 00:29:22,533
- [Crow] It's noon and
he's still fillibustering.

735
00:29:22,533 --> 00:29:25,933
- [Joel] (ebbs
and awws) Pick me.

736
00:29:25,933 --> 00:29:27,367
(ebbs and awws)

737
00:29:27,367 --> 00:29:30,000
- It's not a simple job.

738
00:29:30,000 --> 00:29:32,567
Not everyone has
the strength for it.

739
00:29:32,567 --> 00:29:35,567
We must test each man to see.

740
00:29:35,567 --> 00:29:37,333
If you wish to go on the journey

741
00:29:37,333 --> 00:29:39,067
then you must pass the test.

742
00:29:39,067 --> 00:29:42,100
- [Tom] Not everyone is cut
out to be an Arby's fry cook.

743
00:29:42,100 --> 00:29:44,633
- [Crow] Tonight,
Cannon goes undercover.

744
00:29:44,633 --> 00:29:46,533
- Collecting an army.

745
00:29:46,533 --> 00:29:47,700
Form against us?

746
00:29:47,700 --> 00:29:49,200
- Let him.

747
00:29:49,200 --> 00:29:51,267
We should soon have his
head for all his follies.

748
00:29:51,267 --> 00:29:52,733
- Not soon enough.

749
00:29:52,733 --> 00:29:54,500
- [Joel] Still, it
was a good speech.

750
00:29:54,500 --> 00:29:56,133
- [Sinbad] Roll out
a barrel of wine

751
00:29:56,133 --> 00:29:57,467
and the large drinking cup.

752
00:29:57,467 --> 00:29:58,800
♪ We'll have a barrel of fun.

753
00:29:58,800 --> 00:30:02,133
- Plenty enough for all of you.

754
00:30:02,133 --> 00:30:03,067
- [Joel] Everyone dresses like

755
00:30:03,067 --> 00:30:05,833
Michael Nesmith in this town.

756
00:30:05,833 --> 00:30:07,267
- Who will be first to try?

757
00:30:07,267 --> 00:30:08,900
Step up here.

758
00:30:08,900 --> 00:30:10,467
- I hear the call.

759
00:30:10,467 --> 00:30:11,733
Let me have it.

760
00:30:11,733 --> 00:30:12,967
- Drink.

761
00:30:12,967 --> 00:30:15,100
- [Crow] They're test
marketing Crystal Pepsi.

762
00:30:15,100 --> 00:30:18,933
- [Tom] Sinbad and
Friends, The College Years.

763
00:30:20,333 --> 00:30:22,000
Foster Brooks,
ladies and gentleman.

764
00:30:22,000 --> 00:30:23,167
Foster Brooks.

765
00:30:24,633 --> 00:30:26,100
- And now you try.

766
00:30:26,100 --> 00:30:27,633
- I'm ready.

767
00:30:27,633 --> 00:30:29,433
- [Crow] The Alcoholic
Voyage of Sinbad

768
00:30:29,433 --> 00:30:31,033
will be back after this.

769
00:30:31,033 --> 00:30:34,233
- [Joel] Gulp, gulp, gulp, gulp.

770
00:30:34,233 --> 00:30:35,633
- Good man.

771
00:30:35,633 --> 00:30:37,467
Are you prepared to
stand up to one blow?

772
00:30:37,467 --> 00:30:38,300
- Do it.

773
00:30:40,533 --> 00:30:41,733
- [Tom] Ow, couldn't he have

774
00:30:41,733 --> 00:30:42,967
guessed your weight
or something?

775
00:30:42,967 --> 00:30:44,800
- Let's see if I
can stand the blow.

776
00:30:44,800 --> 00:30:46,800
- Alright, Kaseem,
here is your drink.

777
00:30:46,800 --> 00:30:48,067
- [Tom] His guest.

778
00:30:48,067 --> 00:30:49,333
- [Crow] This is
how they selected

779
00:30:49,333 --> 00:30:52,067
the jury for the
Rodney King trial.

780
00:30:52,067 --> 00:30:53,533
- Bravely done.

781
00:30:53,533 --> 00:30:56,700
If I knock you down, good
Kaseem, don't bear me a grudge.

782
00:30:56,700 --> 00:30:59,467
- Alright, see if you
can knock me down.

783
00:30:59,467 --> 00:31:02,767
- [Joel] How about a
nice Hawaiian punch?

784
00:31:02,767 --> 00:31:04,933
- You're a good man, Kaseem.

785
00:31:04,933 --> 00:31:06,433
Are there more of
suspended belief?

786
00:31:06,433 --> 00:31:09,700
- [Viewers] We're gonna
make it after all.

787
00:31:09,700 --> 00:31:12,233
- [Joel] Sinbad thinks
of all the fun stuff.

788
00:31:12,233 --> 00:31:14,833
- [Tom] Ow, ow, ow, ow, ow, ow.

789
00:31:18,367 --> 00:31:19,633
- You pass the test.

790
00:31:19,633 --> 00:31:21,833
- [Crow] SAT's were
different back then.

791
00:31:21,833 --> 00:31:23,200
- I am ready for the test.

792
00:31:23,200 --> 00:31:25,033
- No need, you pass without it.

793
00:31:25,033 --> 00:31:27,333
- Well, but free wine
is hard to come by.

794
00:31:27,333 --> 00:31:29,800
- [Crow] How about just
knee him in the groin then?

795
00:31:29,800 --> 00:31:31,300
- Well said.

796
00:31:31,300 --> 00:31:34,933
- [Tom] He's drinking out
of a Captain Crunch hat.

797
00:31:34,933 --> 00:31:36,967
- [Crow] There's a
squirrel in there.

798
00:31:36,967 --> 00:31:38,367
Look at that.

799
00:31:38,367 --> 00:31:39,800
- No, hit me too.

800
00:31:42,167 --> 00:31:45,000
- That would be the day,
when a fist hurt him.

801
00:31:45,000 --> 00:31:47,733
Better hit him with a
cudgel or else nothing.

802
00:31:47,733 --> 00:31:50,933
- [Crow] Grover always comes
up with the real zinger.

803
00:31:50,933 --> 00:31:52,700
- And I'm still involved.

804
00:31:52,700 --> 00:31:53,533
- I'll tell you.

805
00:31:53,533 --> 00:31:55,100
Let him fight my bear.

806
00:31:55,100 --> 00:31:57,200
Then you'll see a really
good match here, hey?

807
00:31:57,200 --> 00:31:58,700
- I'll give you a better fight.

808
00:31:58,700 --> 00:32:00,300
Why not?

809
00:32:00,300 --> 00:32:01,533
- [Tom] Hey, nobody
ever asked me

810
00:32:01,533 --> 00:32:03,967
if I wanted to be
a part of this.

811
00:32:05,100 --> 00:32:08,700
- [Crow] The bear's
going into rope-a-dope.

812
00:32:08,700 --> 00:32:10,267
- Come on, you fur rug.

813
00:32:10,267 --> 00:32:11,600
- [Joel] Check it out.

814
00:32:11,600 --> 00:32:13,567
The bear's having an
intervention with Dan Haggerty.

815
00:32:13,567 --> 00:32:15,233
- [Tom] Dan, I
wouldn't confront you

816
00:32:15,233 --> 00:32:18,300
like this if I didn't
care about you.

817
00:32:19,467 --> 00:32:21,167
- [Crow] See, Dan,
even Denver Pyle

818
00:32:21,167 --> 00:32:22,533
and his family showed up.

819
00:32:22,533 --> 00:32:25,200
They want you to seek help, too.

820
00:32:25,200 --> 00:32:26,733
- [Tom] I love you, damn it.

821
00:32:26,733 --> 00:32:30,100
Danny, can't you see that
you're destroying yourself?

822
00:32:30,100 --> 00:32:30,933
Come on!

823
00:32:32,333 --> 00:32:34,600
- [Crow] Listen, Haggerty,
you can fight me and run away

824
00:32:34,600 --> 00:32:36,633
but you can never run
away from yourself.

825
00:32:36,633 --> 00:32:38,033
- Enough, you'll kill him.

826
00:32:38,033 --> 00:32:40,367
Get off, you brute, get off.

827
00:32:41,667 --> 00:32:44,067
- [Joel] It's been a fun day.

828
00:32:46,133 --> 00:32:48,000
- You're a strong
man indeed, Thomas.

829
00:32:48,000 --> 00:32:50,867
- [Tom] Wish I could hire ya.

830
00:32:50,867 --> 00:32:54,100
- Hey, Sinbad, would
ya take me with you?

831
00:32:54,100 --> 00:32:55,700
- [Crow] Let me explain
it one more time.

832
00:32:55,700 --> 00:32:57,000
No.

833
00:32:57,000 --> 00:32:58,300
- You're a little
too weak, I fear.

834
00:32:58,300 --> 00:32:59,700
- [Joel] Oh, that
was uncalled for.

835
00:32:59,700 --> 00:33:02,700
- I think you'll find me
valuable if you try me.

836
00:33:02,700 --> 00:33:04,033
You see, I do many things.

837
00:33:04,033 --> 00:33:06,133
Things that other men cannot do.

838
00:33:06,133 --> 00:33:08,533
You see that I'm wily
and clever with my hands.

839
00:33:08,533 --> 00:33:10,267
Strength is not all.

840
00:33:10,267 --> 00:33:11,633
What do you see here?

841
00:33:11,633 --> 00:33:14,367
- [Tom] I see a
suspicious stain.

842
00:33:15,867 --> 00:33:17,933
- [Joel] He's a demon!

843
00:33:17,933 --> 00:33:19,967
- Alright, Tripod,
you'll join us

844
00:33:19,967 --> 00:33:21,767
and we're happy to have you.

845
00:33:21,767 --> 00:33:23,233
- [Crow] Put him
on another ship.

846
00:33:23,233 --> 00:33:25,233
- And now, friends,
get me a net.

847
00:33:25,233 --> 00:33:27,100
A silken one to catch the bait.

848
00:33:27,100 --> 00:33:28,600
The time has come.

849
00:33:28,600 --> 00:33:30,233
- [Tom] You know, guys, this
doesn't seem like Persia,

850
00:33:30,233 --> 00:33:32,200
and it's probably
not even Sinbad.

851
00:33:32,200 --> 00:33:34,300
- The sun has long been up.

852
00:33:34,300 --> 00:33:37,300
(retro '80's music)

853
00:33:40,833 --> 00:33:44,267
- [Crow] What the
samscratch is going on?

854
00:33:45,767 --> 00:33:47,333
- [Joel] You know he never
really goes out to sea.

855
00:33:47,333 --> 00:33:49,967
He just goes out a little ways.

856
00:33:49,967 --> 00:33:53,633
- [Crow] These are the
fabulous golden fish.

857
00:33:55,100 --> 00:33:56,567
- [Tom] Hey, a
whole bunch of fish.

858
00:33:56,567 --> 00:33:58,833
You can all go home now.

859
00:33:58,833 --> 00:34:01,067
- [Joel] Spectator fishing.

860
00:34:03,167 --> 00:34:06,300
- [Crow] Just some syringes
and Coney Island whitefish.

861
00:34:06,300 --> 00:34:08,800
- [Tom] He can say
goodbye to his head now.

862
00:34:08,800 --> 00:34:09,800
- [Crow] I'm dead.

863
00:34:09,800 --> 00:34:11,100
- No luck.
- Whoohah!

864
00:34:11,100 --> 00:34:12,600
- [Joel] The hell?

865
00:34:13,533 --> 00:34:15,367
- [Spectator] No fish.

866
00:34:17,000 --> 00:34:19,167
- [Joel] Still it's
a nice day to be out.

867
00:34:19,167 --> 00:34:21,400
- [Crow] How long do I get?

868
00:34:24,300 --> 00:34:25,833
- [Joel] Oh, there goes a
tag going right through.

869
00:34:25,833 --> 00:34:27,100
- [Tom] There he
goes again, guys.

870
00:34:27,100 --> 00:34:27,933
Look out.

871
00:34:29,267 --> 00:34:31,433
- [Crow] This is
it, the big one.

872
00:34:31,433 --> 00:34:32,967
Do bullheads count?

873
00:34:32,967 --> 00:34:34,467
Darn.

874
00:34:34,467 --> 00:34:36,667
- [Joel] What is this?

875
00:34:36,667 --> 00:34:39,700
- Upick, this man
holds no gold fin fish.

876
00:34:39,700 --> 00:34:41,900
- [Tom] You a Yukon
Cornelius over here?

877
00:34:41,900 --> 00:34:43,067
- [Crow] And the
crowd settles in

878
00:34:43,067 --> 00:34:45,833
after a disappointing
first half.

879
00:34:47,133 --> 00:34:49,300
- [Tom] Three weeks later.

880
00:34:52,600 --> 00:34:56,667
- [Joel] Wait 'til
they get a load of me.

881
00:34:56,667 --> 00:34:59,500
- [Crow] Get along,
little fishies, yeehaw.

882
00:34:59,500 --> 00:35:02,667
Really stunk it up
in here, pesto burp.

883
00:35:02,667 --> 00:35:03,667
Sorry, fish.

884
00:35:05,867 --> 00:35:07,767
- [Joel] Please, oh please,
oh please, oh please.

885
00:35:07,767 --> 00:35:10,833
- Princess, you
haven't forgotten me.

886
00:35:12,433 --> 00:35:13,433
- Beautiful.

887
00:35:14,367 --> 00:35:15,900
- I won, I won!

888
00:35:15,900 --> 00:35:16,967
- [Crow] We have a winner.

889
00:35:16,967 --> 00:35:17,800
Hold your cards.

890
00:35:17,800 --> 00:35:19,567
- Sinbad has done it.

891
00:35:20,600 --> 00:35:24,600
♪ We're gonna make it after all

892
00:35:25,600 --> 00:35:26,833
- He's done it.

893
00:35:28,267 --> 00:35:29,700
- [Joel] So does
anybody see anything

894
00:35:29,700 --> 00:35:32,267
in this movie remotely Arabian?

895
00:35:33,700 --> 00:35:37,267
- [Crow] Hurray, what's a
fish gonna do for us again?

896
00:35:37,267 --> 00:35:38,867
Give it up for me, I won!

897
00:35:38,867 --> 00:35:39,700
Whoo!

898
00:35:40,967 --> 00:35:42,433
- You've lost your
wager, merchants,

899
00:35:42,433 --> 00:35:43,867
and now you must give
your goods to Sinbad and--

900
00:35:43,867 --> 00:35:47,033
- [Joel] Ah, jam it,
you crummy prole.

901
00:35:50,500 --> 00:35:52,633
- [Tom] Here it is,
thank you, keep it up.

902
00:35:52,633 --> 00:35:53,600
Keep it going for me.

903
00:35:53,600 --> 00:35:54,433
Come on.

904
00:35:55,500 --> 00:35:57,033
It's me.

905
00:35:57,033 --> 00:35:58,567
- [Crow] Uh-oh, what's the
clearance on that bridge?

906
00:35:58,567 --> 00:36:02,400
- [Tom] I don't know, I
think it's about 13'9.

907
00:36:03,367 --> 00:36:04,767
- [Joel] This is turning out to

908
00:36:04,767 --> 00:36:07,500
be one heck of a
portage, yes, it's me!

909
00:36:07,500 --> 00:36:08,967
Hello.

910
00:36:08,967 --> 00:36:10,967
- [Crow] Kiss my big,
white, Sinbad butt, I won.

911
00:36:10,967 --> 00:36:13,633
Whoo-hoo!
- Who's gonna clean it?

912
00:36:14,700 --> 00:36:16,667
- Phooey.
- I'm going home.

913
00:36:21,533 --> 00:36:24,200
- [Joel] Your Persian Clippers

914
00:36:24,200 --> 00:36:28,700
returning home after
winning the World Series.

915
00:36:28,700 --> 00:36:31,567
- Why do you have such
glum faces, my gents?

916
00:36:31,567 --> 00:36:33,767
Don't you think I look
better with my head?

917
00:36:33,767 --> 00:36:36,000
- [Joel] Yeah, let's try
it the other way and see.

918
00:36:36,000 --> 00:36:39,733
- Hand over the keys to
all of your warehouses.

919
00:36:39,733 --> 00:36:43,467
- [Crow] Now give me your pin
numbers for your bank cards.

920
00:36:43,467 --> 00:36:45,000
- Here now, my worthy crew,

921
00:36:45,000 --> 00:36:48,000
take these keys
and open the shops.

922
00:36:48,000 --> 00:36:51,367
Get yourselves clothes
and new sharp swords.

923
00:36:51,367 --> 00:36:55,000
Then give new
clothes to everyone.

924
00:36:55,000 --> 00:36:56,100
- [Tom] I'm a 44 long.

925
00:36:56,100 --> 00:36:58,600
- Clothes, food, and fuel.

926
00:36:58,600 --> 00:37:01,000
All this give to the poor.

927
00:37:01,000 --> 00:37:03,067
The silk and the velvet cloth,

928
00:37:03,067 --> 00:37:06,367
all this give them and let
them know how it is to be rich.

929
00:37:06,367 --> 00:37:08,033
- [Joel] Alright, and
stock up on socks.

930
00:37:08,033 --> 00:37:10,833
You know you're never gonna
have this chance again.

931
00:37:10,833 --> 00:37:14,267
- [Crow] It's just a
band aid for the economy.

932
00:37:14,267 --> 00:37:17,600
- [Joel] These people,
any excuse to squat.

933
00:37:17,600 --> 00:37:20,700
- [Tom] This is like
Sturgess before motorcycles.

934
00:37:20,700 --> 00:37:21,933
- [Joel] You know, I
can't tell if that's a

935
00:37:21,933 --> 00:37:25,133
Magritte or if that's
a hole in the wall?

936
00:37:27,733 --> 00:37:31,767
- [Crow] Hey, Mr. Tambourine
Man, play a song for me.

937
00:37:31,767 --> 00:37:32,900
- [Joel] Boy, life
is sure better

938
00:37:32,900 --> 00:37:34,900
since that one fish got here.

939
00:37:34,900 --> 00:37:36,167
- [Crow] Yeah, wonder what they

940
00:37:36,167 --> 00:37:38,000
would've done for
a lobster dinner.

941
00:37:38,000 --> 00:37:39,267
- [Tom] Let's see,
before Sinbad came,

942
00:37:39,267 --> 00:37:41,067
everybody was partying
and after Sinbad came,

943
00:37:41,067 --> 00:37:42,267
everybody's partying.

944
00:37:42,267 --> 00:37:45,300
He's changed a whole
here, didn't he?

945
00:37:46,500 --> 00:37:49,267
- [Crow] Tad, don't
ever do that again.

946
00:37:49,267 --> 00:37:53,800
- [Joel] Man, I never knew
Arabia was so Russian.

947
00:37:53,800 --> 00:37:55,600
- [Crow] Well maybe this
was a finished movie called

948
00:37:55,600 --> 00:37:58,000
"The Magic Voyage of Torvil".

949
00:38:00,300 --> 00:38:03,200
- [Tom] It's Dance Party Persia.

950
00:38:03,200 --> 00:38:04,100
Or Finland.

951
00:38:06,433 --> 00:38:11,067
- [Crow] Nobody ever
picked me for basketball.

952
00:38:11,067 --> 00:38:13,500
- Hey Tripod--
- Tripod?

953
00:38:13,500 --> 00:38:15,533
- Why aren't you singing
and dancing like the others?

954
00:38:15,533 --> 00:38:16,867
Have a good time.

955
00:38:16,867 --> 00:38:18,333
- You must forgive me.

956
00:38:18,333 --> 00:38:19,633
I do not feel like dancing.

957
00:38:19,633 --> 00:38:23,867
♪ I do not feel like dancing

958
00:38:23,867 --> 00:38:25,733
- Why shouldn't the
people enjoy themselves?

959
00:38:25,733 --> 00:38:27,867
Look how happy everyone is.

960
00:38:27,867 --> 00:38:29,700
There's no hunger, or poverty.

961
00:38:29,700 --> 00:38:31,067
They have happiness.

962
00:38:31,067 --> 00:38:32,933
- What is it with your soul?

963
00:38:32,933 --> 00:38:35,800
Take a troubled look beyond
your nose at what you see--

964
00:38:35,800 --> 00:38:37,267
- [Tom] Geez, even when
Paris was liberated,

965
00:38:37,267 --> 00:38:39,967
this guy brought 'em all down.

966
00:38:39,967 --> 00:38:41,233
- [Crow] Oh yeah, that.

967
00:38:41,233 --> 00:38:43,233
- Keep looking there.
- Oh yeah, I've seen it.

968
00:38:43,233 --> 00:38:45,400
- [Tom] Come on, take
a big, steamy gawk.

969
00:38:45,400 --> 00:38:46,833
- I'm looking.
- Come on, look. Look.

970
00:38:46,833 --> 00:38:47,800
- Stop it.
- Look.

971
00:38:47,800 --> 00:38:49,067
- Stop it!
- Look.

972
00:38:52,233 --> 00:38:54,567
- [Crow] They were sold out.

973
00:38:56,267 --> 00:38:59,767
- [Joel] Could you catch
another fish, please?

974
00:38:59,767 --> 00:39:01,433
- Who are they?

975
00:39:01,433 --> 00:39:02,433
- The lost ones.

976
00:39:02,433 --> 00:39:03,267
They heard
- Jason Patrick,

977
00:39:03,267 --> 00:39:04,600
Kiefer Sutherland?

978
00:39:04,600 --> 00:39:06,100
- You've given
everything, everything

979
00:39:06,100 --> 00:39:08,267
you had away to the people here

980
00:39:08,267 --> 00:39:10,367
and still there is no happiness.

981
00:39:10,367 --> 00:39:11,567
- [Crow] Your point, please?

982
00:39:11,567 --> 00:39:13,500
- Now there is no money
to build your ships.

983
00:39:13,500 --> 00:39:14,800
- I muddled my own plan.

984
00:39:14,800 --> 00:39:17,267
- [Joel] You muddied
your own pants?

985
00:39:17,267 --> 00:39:19,300
- I just wanted to
give happiness to them.

986
00:39:19,300 --> 00:39:21,300
- [Tom] Well you didn't.

987
00:39:22,500 --> 00:39:26,800
- [Crow] Look, go ruin
another town's economy.

988
00:39:26,800 --> 00:39:29,467
- [Joel] And stay out, Sinbad.

989
00:39:29,467 --> 00:39:32,300
(Crow fake cries)

990
00:39:34,067 --> 00:39:36,067
- [Crow] I'm not crying.

991
00:39:37,033 --> 00:39:38,033
- Lubiria.

992
00:39:38,033 --> 00:39:38,967
- [Tom] Great job, Sinbad.

993
00:39:38,967 --> 00:39:41,067
You really humiliated me today.

994
00:39:41,067 --> 00:39:43,600
- I was almost afraid
you weren't coming.

995
00:39:43,600 --> 00:39:45,900
- I had trouble getting
away from Mother.

996
00:39:45,900 --> 00:39:48,867
- [Joel] And my boyfriend
is waiting in the car.

997
00:39:48,867 --> 00:39:50,767
- Did you tell your
Mother of my love for you?

998
00:39:50,767 --> 00:39:53,200
- [Crow] No, you
think I'm stupid?

999
00:39:53,200 --> 00:39:55,533
- She says I haven't
known you long enough.

1000
00:39:55,533 --> 00:39:58,267
You're a seaman, and the
sea has no place for me.

1001
00:39:58,267 --> 00:39:59,933
- [Tom] And she brought
up the fish thing, too.

1002
00:39:59,933 --> 00:40:01,300
- What can I do?

1003
00:40:01,300 --> 00:40:03,033
You must see my position.

1004
00:40:03,033 --> 00:40:05,600
- [Crow] Is she laying him off?

1005
00:40:07,133 --> 00:40:09,400
- We can no longer
see one another.

1006
00:40:09,400 --> 00:40:12,500
- [Joel] This pretty much fits
with the rest of my day, gah.

1007
00:40:12,500 --> 00:40:16,800
- [Tom] Well it's early,
I can still see Debbie.

1008
00:40:16,800 --> 00:40:18,433
- That's not what I say.

1009
00:40:18,433 --> 00:40:20,567
That's what my
Mother said to me.

1010
00:40:20,567 --> 00:40:24,500
- [Crow] Your mother doesn't
want to see me anymore?

1011
00:40:24,500 --> 00:40:26,567
- I'll always be proud
of what you have done.

1012
00:40:26,567 --> 00:40:28,467
You don't have to become rich.

1013
00:40:28,467 --> 00:40:30,100
I only want you.

1014
00:40:30,100 --> 00:40:31,267
- [Joel] And a tetherball.

1015
00:40:31,267 --> 00:40:33,300
- I know you, Sinbad.

1016
00:40:33,300 --> 00:40:36,400
I believe I can make you happy.

1017
00:40:36,400 --> 00:40:38,700
So you see, you must let me.

1018
00:40:40,200 --> 00:40:42,633
- [Tom] Oh, oh, sorry, I
was thinking about my hat.

1019
00:40:42,633 --> 00:40:43,833
- But I must leave you shortly.

1020
00:40:43,833 --> 00:40:45,067
- [Tom] Oh, and that golden fish

1021
00:40:45,067 --> 00:40:46,233
isn't agreeing with me at all.

1022
00:40:46,233 --> 00:40:48,167
- I have to make my journey.

1023
00:40:48,167 --> 00:40:49,433
- What journey?

1024
00:40:49,433 --> 00:40:50,267
- [Tom] You know,
the big journey.

1025
00:40:50,267 --> 00:40:52,100
- I promised the people.

1026
00:40:52,100 --> 00:40:54,167
I must search for
their happiness.

1027
00:40:54,167 --> 00:40:58,367
- I pray first that you
will find our happiness.

1028
00:40:58,367 --> 00:41:01,867
But if theirs is more
important, remember--

1029
00:41:01,867 --> 00:41:03,033
- [Joel] Don't flush q-tips.

1030
00:41:03,033 --> 00:41:05,433
- First and last, I am yours.

1031
00:41:08,133 --> 00:41:11,367
- [Tom] Oh, whoopeedink,
Sinbad's back.

1032
00:41:12,800 --> 00:41:16,967
- [Crow] Wanna get another
softball game going?

1033
00:41:16,967 --> 00:41:20,367
Made my own
blender-aise last night.

1034
00:41:20,367 --> 00:41:21,967
Turned out pretty creamy.

1035
00:41:21,967 --> 00:41:24,300
- [Joel] Hey, those
are from Pier One.

1036
00:41:24,300 --> 00:41:26,333
- [Tom] Bet they're really
stinking up the place by now.

1037
00:41:26,333 --> 00:41:28,500
- A harvest of foolishness
I've left myself.

1038
00:41:28,500 --> 00:41:29,567
- [Joel] Yup.

1039
00:41:31,467 --> 00:41:34,700
- [Crow] She's playing
with bath beads.

1040
00:41:35,867 --> 00:41:39,067
- [Tom] Brought to
you in living color.

1041
00:41:42,867 --> 00:41:45,533
- [Crow] Suddenly sushi?

1042
00:41:45,533 --> 00:41:47,000
(laughs)

1043
00:41:47,000 --> 00:41:48,233
Great.

1044
00:41:48,233 --> 00:41:51,700
- [Tom] The power of
creative visualization.

1045
00:41:52,600 --> 00:41:54,667
- Ah, Princess, I thank you.

1046
00:41:54,667 --> 00:41:55,900
- [Crow] Oh fun.

1047
00:41:55,900 --> 00:41:57,200
- [Tom] Hi, I also
ironed your work shirt

1048
00:41:57,200 --> 00:41:59,467
and packed your lunch, too.

1049
00:42:00,400 --> 00:42:01,867
- My friends, wake up.

1050
00:42:01,867 --> 00:42:04,800
(retro 80's music)

1051
00:42:08,167 --> 00:42:10,633
(cavemen grunting)

1052
00:42:10,633 --> 00:42:13,300
(robot giggles)

1053
00:42:14,667 --> 00:42:17,733
- We were wondering
what would you do

1054
00:42:17,733 --> 00:42:20,067
if Sinbad came to your town?

1055
00:42:21,967 --> 00:42:24,367
Wouldn't you want the
City Council to do
something about it?

1056
00:42:24,367 --> 00:42:26,167
Let's watch.

1057
00:42:26,167 --> 00:42:28,233
- [Joel] Okay, beardheads,
floor is resolved.

1058
00:42:28,233 --> 00:42:32,733
Parking is diagonal rather than
parallel in downtown Persia.

1059
00:42:32,733 --> 00:42:35,600
Next item, can I get
some water, please?

1060
00:42:35,600 --> 00:42:37,767
- Mr. President.
- You're the President?

1061
00:42:37,767 --> 00:42:39,467
- Sure, why not?

1062
00:42:39,467 --> 00:42:40,867
- Then can I be Labor
MP from Brixton.

1063
00:42:40,867 --> 00:42:44,700
- Yes, the President recognizes
the Honorable Tom Servo.

1064
00:42:44,700 --> 00:42:47,767
- Thank you, and gentlemen,
the Sinbad problem--

1065
00:42:47,767 --> 00:42:49,367
- Move the table,
he's not Sinbad.

1066
00:42:49,367 --> 00:42:51,133
- Motion is out of order.

1067
00:42:51,133 --> 00:42:52,833
I've not yet yielded the floor.

1068
00:42:52,833 --> 00:42:55,033
My honorable
colleagues, and Crow,

1069
00:42:55,033 --> 00:42:58,233
far too long have we denied
the existence of this scourge.

1070
00:42:58,233 --> 00:42:59,433
- What a cheap demagogue.

1071
00:42:59,433 --> 00:43:01,033
Servo, you're a cheap demagogue.

1072
00:43:01,033 --> 00:43:04,800
- Be it demagoguery, sir, to
safeguard the public morals?

1073
00:43:04,800 --> 00:43:06,700
Item one, Sinbad
has continually,

1074
00:43:06,700 --> 00:43:10,300
and in clear violation
of City Statute 101.4563,

1075
00:43:10,300 --> 00:43:13,700
1998 Statutes Amended,
interrupted our daily routine.

1076
00:43:13,700 --> 00:43:15,067
- He's not Sinbad.

1077
00:43:15,067 --> 00:43:16,767
- Gentleman, I'm a
fellow what likes

1078
00:43:16,767 --> 00:43:19,033
to know what he's doing
and when he's doing it.

1079
00:43:19,033 --> 00:43:21,933
Ours is a society based
on ancient traditions.

1080
00:43:21,933 --> 00:43:23,533
- I thought we just
sold each other fish.

1081
00:43:23,533 --> 00:43:24,833
- That's what I thought, too.

1082
00:43:24,833 --> 00:43:26,067
Ooh, I got one.

1083
00:43:26,067 --> 00:43:27,767
Could I have some
more water, please?

1084
00:43:27,767 --> 00:43:29,733
- And most pressing
on the public coffers,

1085
00:43:29,733 --> 00:43:32,100
why in God's name is
Sinbad tax exempt?

1086
00:43:32,100 --> 00:43:33,500
- Look, do you
have a suggestion?

1087
00:43:33,500 --> 00:43:34,933
- Yes, banishment!

1088
00:43:34,933 --> 00:43:38,867
- Okay, the President recognizes
the Labor MP from Brixton.

1089
00:43:38,867 --> 00:43:40,067
- Thank you.

1090
00:43:40,067 --> 00:43:41,600
Move to refer whole
issue to zoning.

1091
00:43:41,600 --> 00:43:44,267
Move to find out what the
heck is with these beards.

1092
00:43:44,267 --> 00:43:48,100
And move to find out the true
identity of this guy, Skinbag.

1093
00:43:48,100 --> 00:43:51,867
- (chuckles) You mean Zigzag?

1094
00:43:51,867 --> 00:43:53,800
- Precisely, Whizbang.

1095
00:43:53,800 --> 00:43:57,033
- Gentlemen, you'll
ruin our infrastructure.

1096
00:43:57,033 --> 00:43:58,733
- Move to end sketch.
- Oh yes.

1097
00:43:58,733 --> 00:43:59,567
Do I hear a second?

1098
00:43:59,567 --> 00:44:00,567
- I second.

1099
00:44:00,567 --> 00:44:01,367
- Is there any discussion?

1100
00:44:01,367 --> 00:44:02,800
- Yeah, he's not Sinbad.

1101
00:44:02,800 --> 00:44:03,733
- So ordered.

1102
00:44:03,733 --> 00:44:04,667
Could I get some water, please?

1103
00:44:04,667 --> 00:44:07,333
- I'll get the water for ya.

1104
00:44:07,333 --> 00:44:08,433
- Sometimes lost causes are the

1105
00:44:08,433 --> 00:44:10,900
only causes worth fighting for.

1106
00:44:10,900 --> 00:44:11,967
(sirens)

1107
00:44:11,967 --> 00:44:12,900
No, movie time!

1108
00:44:12,900 --> 00:44:16,667
(doors sliding and slamming)

1109
00:44:21,833 --> 00:44:24,133
- Tinpans.
- Semenblend.

1110
00:44:24,133 --> 00:44:25,633
- [Joel] Skinsnag.

1111
00:44:25,633 --> 00:44:27,800
- Just look at this gold
we received from the sea.

1112
00:44:27,800 --> 00:44:29,667
- [Crow] Welcome to
Manic Depressiveville.

1113
00:44:29,667 --> 00:44:30,733
- Look, look.

1114
00:44:30,733 --> 00:44:33,167
Each man take some at once.

1115
00:44:33,167 --> 00:44:34,900
- [Joel] What is he, Percy Ross?

1116
00:44:34,900 --> 00:44:37,267
- [Sinbad] We must
have ships at once.

1117
00:44:37,267 --> 00:44:40,600
Strong, fast ships to carry us
on our search for happiness.

1118
00:44:40,600 --> 00:44:43,933
- [Joel] It's a
rack of bronto ribs.

1119
00:44:43,933 --> 00:44:47,100
- [Sinbad] We will not return
until happiness is ours,

1120
00:44:47,100 --> 00:44:48,500
however long it takes us.

1121
00:44:48,500 --> 00:44:50,800
Hurry, the sea waits for us.

1122
00:44:52,100 --> 00:44:53,633
- [Tom] My aunt lives out there.

1123
00:44:53,633 --> 00:44:55,867
- [Crow] Sinbad-tested,
God-approved.

1124
00:44:55,867 --> 00:44:58,267
(epic music)

1125
00:45:02,600 --> 00:45:05,833
- [Tom] And now
intermission, Part Two.

1126
00:45:05,833 --> 00:45:07,967
- [Joel] Well this is it.

1127
00:45:07,967 --> 00:45:09,433
- [Tom] This is a really
a dumb relationship.

1128
00:45:09,433 --> 00:45:13,433
They haven't gone to a Dairy
Queen, or a movie, or anything.

1129
00:45:13,433 --> 00:45:15,367
- Wait patiently
for me, loved one.

1130
00:45:15,367 --> 00:45:16,600
Remember--

1131
00:45:16,600 --> 00:45:19,533
- [Crow] Don't eat
refrozen ice cream.

1132
00:45:21,233 --> 00:45:23,067
- Of the Earth itself.

1133
00:45:24,567 --> 00:45:25,933
I will come back to you.

1134
00:45:25,933 --> 00:45:27,133
- [Tom] Stay alive.

1135
00:45:27,133 --> 00:45:29,400
Whatever may occur,
I will find you.

1136
00:45:29,400 --> 00:45:31,367
- Look, there they are.

1137
00:45:31,367 --> 00:45:33,133
- [Joel] He better join 'em.

1138
00:45:33,133 --> 00:45:34,967
- The birds of love.

1139
00:45:34,967 --> 00:45:38,067
I will send one
after you every year.

1140
00:45:38,067 --> 00:45:40,000
- [Crow] I want you to
have this rear view mirror.

1141
00:45:40,000 --> 00:45:41,667
- If you wear this
amulet, I'll feel safer.

1142
00:45:41,667 --> 00:45:46,267
- [Tom] It's a Denver
amulet (laughs).

1143
00:45:46,267 --> 00:45:47,100
- You're a good man--

1144
00:45:47,100 --> 00:45:49,000
- [Joel] Charlie Brown.

1145
00:45:51,333 --> 00:45:53,000
- Now you should go.

1146
00:45:54,700 --> 00:45:55,933
My own beloved.

1147
00:45:55,933 --> 00:45:57,800
- [Crow] It's just a
business trip, honey.

1148
00:45:57,800 --> 00:45:59,300
- I will not weep.

1149
00:46:01,600 --> 00:46:03,233
I love you very much.

1150
00:46:03,233 --> 00:46:06,333
- [Tom] I love pancakes more.

1151
00:46:06,333 --> 00:46:09,500
- [Joel] Hey, he's
got a Stratego hat.

1152
00:46:11,167 --> 00:46:13,333
♪ And I ran

1153
00:46:13,333 --> 00:46:16,333
♪ I ran so far away

1154
00:46:20,133 --> 00:46:21,367
- [Crow] Now I
always thought Sinbad

1155
00:46:21,367 --> 00:46:24,033
wore big genie pants and
a vest with no shirt.

1156
00:46:24,033 --> 00:46:25,567
- [Joel] Oh well.

1157
00:46:25,567 --> 00:46:26,767
- [Tom] Oh geez, Sinbad doesn't

1158
00:46:26,767 --> 00:46:28,667
make a big deal about
anything, does he?

1159
00:46:28,667 --> 00:46:30,867
- You must not be
angry with us, Sinbad.

1160
00:46:30,867 --> 00:46:32,467
- We only did what
we thought was right.

1161
00:46:32,467 --> 00:46:34,500
- Now you have shown us wisdom.

1162
00:46:34,500 --> 00:46:36,300
- Just go.
- Freedom.

1163
00:46:36,300 --> 00:46:37,967
- I'm not one to harbor
grudges for long.

1164
00:46:37,967 --> 00:46:39,167
- [Tom] Get out of here.

1165
00:46:39,167 --> 00:46:39,967
- Especially against
rich foolish merchants.

1166
00:46:39,967 --> 00:46:40,967
- [Crow] Take a walk.

1167
00:46:40,967 --> 00:46:42,567
- Know that you really care.

1168
00:46:42,567 --> 00:46:44,800
That you were interested only
in the glory of Copasand.

1169
00:46:44,800 --> 00:46:46,033
- [Joel] Get out.

1170
00:46:46,033 --> 00:46:47,633
- That's true, you're
a hero of Copasand.

1171
00:46:47,633 --> 00:46:48,900
- And if you want
all of our goods--

1172
00:46:48,900 --> 00:46:49,833
- [Tom] Not mine.

1173
00:46:49,833 --> 00:46:51,033
- They're yours to trade with.

1174
00:46:51,033 --> 00:46:52,633
Take them.

1175
00:46:52,633 --> 00:46:56,233
- [Joel] What, is ZZ
Top seeing 'em off?

1176
00:46:56,233 --> 00:46:57,600
- I bid you farewell.

1177
00:46:57,600 --> 00:46:59,067
- [Tom] Just go, Sinbad.

1178
00:46:59,067 --> 00:47:01,733
- And find happiness for us all.

1179
00:47:04,000 --> 00:47:07,167
- [Crow] Hey, look,
the Trojan Turkey.

1180
00:47:09,467 --> 00:47:11,500
- [Joel] Yeah, like
Sinbad goes to the store

1181
00:47:11,500 --> 00:47:14,900
and he's gotta call
a crowd in, you know.

1182
00:47:14,900 --> 00:47:17,100
- [Tom] Thank you.

1183
00:47:17,100 --> 00:47:18,767
Now just the ladies.

1184
00:47:19,867 --> 00:47:21,333
Thank you.

1185
00:47:21,333 --> 00:47:22,833
Thank you.

1186
00:47:22,833 --> 00:47:24,667
- [Crow] Is the crowd moving
or is the platform moving?

1187
00:47:24,667 --> 00:47:27,000
Cause the plot isn't moving.

1188
00:47:28,400 --> 00:47:29,633
- [Tom] I said he could go.

1189
00:47:29,633 --> 00:47:31,167
I didn't think that
he actually would.

1190
00:47:31,167 --> 00:47:34,767
- She's got a clacker hat.
- Oh neat.

1191
00:47:34,767 --> 00:47:37,433
Hey, those ships have scoliosis.

1192
00:47:38,700 --> 00:47:39,633
- [Tom] We're out of the harbor.

1193
00:47:39,633 --> 00:47:41,900
You can stop bowing now, Sinbad.

1194
00:47:41,900 --> 00:47:42,733
- [Joel] Thank you.

1195
00:47:42,733 --> 00:47:43,667
Thank you very much.

1196
00:47:43,667 --> 00:47:45,167
Thank you.

1197
00:47:45,167 --> 00:47:48,133
- [Crow] This is God, now
concluding my broadcast day.

1198
00:47:48,133 --> 00:47:48,967
Boooop.

1199
00:47:53,067 --> 00:47:56,167
- [Joel] She's got dual
overhead tear ducts.

1200
00:47:56,167 --> 00:47:57,400
- [Crow] Handy.

1201
00:47:58,733 --> 00:47:59,800
- [Tom] Intermission.

1202
00:47:59,800 --> 00:48:01,300
And now act three.

1203
00:48:04,500 --> 00:48:06,033
- And so--
(Viewers start)

1204
00:48:06,033 --> 00:48:07,467
- [Crow] Must've missed his cue.

1205
00:48:07,467 --> 00:48:10,533
- Sinbad and his brave
crew set out to sea.

1206
00:48:10,533 --> 00:48:14,367
Far into the mysterious
regions of uncharted lands.

1207
00:48:14,367 --> 00:48:17,867
Far from the familiar faces
and sounds of Copasand.

1208
00:48:17,867 --> 00:48:21,167
Sailing into the troubled
waters of the barbaric dark.

1209
00:48:21,167 --> 00:48:22,400
- [Joel] Sounds
like God picked up

1210
00:48:22,400 --> 00:48:25,067
some extra bucks
doing voiceovers.

1211
00:48:25,067 --> 00:48:28,400
- [Tom] It looks
barbaric, doesn't it?

1212
00:48:28,400 --> 00:48:31,600
- [Joel] Tom Stewart killed me.

1213
00:48:31,600 --> 00:48:34,267
(fake vomiting)

1214
00:48:37,867 --> 00:48:41,500
♪ Toast and marmalade with tea

1215
00:48:41,500 --> 00:48:43,400
♪ Sailing ships upon the sea

1216
00:48:43,400 --> 00:48:45,067
- [Tom] Hey, it's
the guys from town!

1217
00:48:45,067 --> 00:48:47,800
They changed their outfits
right around to the other side.

1218
00:48:47,800 --> 00:48:51,267
- [Crow] Ah yes, the
Vikings of Sinbad.

1219
00:48:51,267 --> 00:48:53,700
- [Tom] The Guns of Navarone.

1220
00:48:58,467 --> 00:49:02,567
- [Joel] Hey, they just
discovered Easter Island.

1221
00:49:03,967 --> 00:49:06,500
- [Crow] Heh, they look
the Knights Who Say Ni.

1222
00:49:06,500 --> 00:49:10,200
- [Tom] Must be an overcrowding
problem on this island.

1223
00:49:10,200 --> 00:49:12,300
- [Joel] Sinbad
thinks he's so tough.

1224
00:49:12,300 --> 00:49:13,767
Oh brother.

1225
00:49:13,767 --> 00:49:17,100
- I think we will find that
we are not welcome here.

1226
00:49:17,100 --> 00:49:19,300
- [Crow] I sent my good
wishes to everybody.

1227
00:49:19,300 --> 00:49:20,667
- We come with
peace in our hearts.

1228
00:49:20,667 --> 00:49:23,567
- [Joel] And ants in our pants.

1229
00:49:23,567 --> 00:49:25,667
- If they wish to
have commerce with us,

1230
00:49:25,667 --> 00:49:28,267
we'll exchange goods
and be on our way.

1231
00:49:28,267 --> 00:49:29,233
- [Tom] Here, hang on
to that for me, will ya?

1232
00:49:29,233 --> 00:49:30,333
Thanks.

1233
00:49:30,333 --> 00:49:31,233
- [Joel] Dingo boots.

1234
00:49:31,233 --> 00:49:32,300
Check it out.

1235
00:49:33,767 --> 00:49:35,900
- Is to see what they know
of the bird of happiness.

1236
00:49:35,900 --> 00:49:37,700
- [Crow] We don't know anything.

1237
00:49:37,700 --> 00:49:39,600
- It's always possible.

1238
00:49:40,767 --> 00:49:44,133
- [Tom] It's like a
collective deer stand.

1239
00:49:45,300 --> 00:49:48,000
- [Joel] I claim
this land for all.

1240
00:49:48,900 --> 00:49:51,800
(Tom and Crow quack)

1241
00:49:51,800 --> 00:49:54,400
- Stop where you are.
- Okay.

1242
00:49:54,400 --> 00:49:56,533
- [Man On Horse] Who has
called you to come here?

1243
00:49:56,533 --> 00:49:59,567
- [Joel] We're discovering you.

1244
00:49:59,567 --> 00:50:02,233
- We arrive without invitation.

1245
00:50:02,233 --> 00:50:04,533
We've come from over the
seas to see your land.

1246
00:50:04,533 --> 00:50:05,667
- [Crow] To see your land.

1247
00:50:05,667 --> 00:50:07,867
- And in friendship, to mingle.

1248
00:50:07,867 --> 00:50:09,167
- [Tom] To get
some phone numbers.

1249
00:50:09,167 --> 00:50:11,533
- You'll see we
are a peaceful lot.

1250
00:50:11,533 --> 00:50:13,867
We hope to trade with you.

1251
00:50:13,867 --> 00:50:15,867
Come forward and
inspect our wares.

1252
00:50:15,867 --> 00:50:18,367
- [Tom] Rumple Minze, anybody?

1253
00:50:18,367 --> 00:50:20,367
- But we wish to be
friends with you.

1254
00:50:20,367 --> 00:50:22,067
- [Man On Horse]
Another step and

1255
00:50:22,067 --> 00:50:25,633
it will be the last
step you ever take here.

1256
00:50:25,633 --> 00:50:29,467
- [Crow] We'll turn ourselves
right around and leave.

1257
00:50:29,467 --> 00:50:30,733
- [Joel] Dig this, watch.

1258
00:50:30,733 --> 00:50:34,767
- Obviously, our host
wants us to leave.

1259
00:50:34,767 --> 00:50:35,967
But tell me one thing--

1260
00:50:35,967 --> 00:50:37,533
- [Tom] Why are you such a jerk?

1261
00:50:37,533 --> 00:50:40,933
- Have you got the
bird of happiness?

1262
00:50:40,933 --> 00:50:43,200
- [Crow] We have a
pretty friendly chicken.

1263
00:50:43,200 --> 00:50:44,833
- Happiness is to kill our foes.

1264
00:50:44,833 --> 00:50:46,133
- What a happiness.

1265
00:50:46,133 --> 00:50:48,533
Who wants that kind of life?

1266
00:50:48,533 --> 00:50:51,433
- We sometimes have to
kill to protect ourselves.

1267
00:50:51,433 --> 00:50:52,900
- [Joel] Could I put this down?

1268
00:50:52,900 --> 00:50:55,067
- As for happiness, never.

1269
00:50:56,933 --> 00:50:59,267
- [Tom] Apparently they
don't know who I am.

1270
00:50:59,267 --> 00:51:00,767
- [Sailor] People who
kill for happiness.

1271
00:51:00,767 --> 00:51:02,800
- [Crow] I heard that.

1272
00:51:02,800 --> 00:51:04,933
- [Man On Horse] They have
turned their backs to us.

1273
00:51:04,933 --> 00:51:06,700
Don't let them off the beach.

1274
00:51:06,700 --> 00:51:08,133
Kill them.
- Okay!

1275
00:51:09,633 --> 00:51:11,900
- Look out!
Sinbad!

1276
00:51:11,900 --> 00:51:13,333
- [Joel] Hey, they're heading
after him with shrimp forks.

1277
00:51:13,333 --> 00:51:16,167
- So the only way you
know is treachery.

1278
00:51:16,167 --> 00:51:18,433
So be it, barbarians.

1279
00:51:18,433 --> 00:51:19,933
The battle begins.

1280
00:51:19,933 --> 00:51:21,667
Come on, men, get them.

1281
00:51:21,667 --> 00:51:23,433
Go on.
- Neat.

1282
00:51:23,433 --> 00:51:24,467
- [Crow] Let's do it, catch me.

1283
00:51:24,467 --> 00:51:25,967
- [Tom] Whoa, huh?

1284
00:51:30,733 --> 00:51:32,100
Hey.
- Hey, neato.

1285
00:51:32,100 --> 00:51:33,100
- [Tom] They can only
do that once, though.

1286
00:51:33,100 --> 00:51:34,667
- [Crow] Yeah.

1287
00:51:34,667 --> 00:51:37,667
- [Joel] Ooh, he's
been caramelized.

1288
00:51:39,067 --> 00:51:41,367
- [Crow] He's hitting
him with his windbreaker.

1289
00:51:41,367 --> 00:51:44,767
- [Tom] Ooh, that zipper hurts.

1290
00:51:44,767 --> 00:51:46,933
(Joel thumps)

1291
00:51:46,933 --> 00:51:48,367
- [Crow] Roll another one.

1292
00:51:48,367 --> 00:51:50,767
(epic music)

1293
00:51:53,733 --> 00:51:57,133
- [Joel] Man, these
guys ae easy to kill.

1294
00:52:04,900 --> 00:52:06,067
- [Crow] Grandpa, no.

1295
00:52:06,067 --> 00:52:07,033
- Where do you
think you're going?

1296
00:52:07,033 --> 00:52:08,233
- My place is with him.

1297
00:52:08,233 --> 00:52:09,267
- You're too young to fight--

1298
00:52:09,267 --> 00:52:11,767
- [Tom] Tim, don't do it, Tim.

1299
00:52:13,933 --> 00:52:15,467
- [Crow] Ohh, ow, my hip.

1300
00:52:15,467 --> 00:52:16,400
Careful.

1301
00:52:16,400 --> 00:52:19,067
- [Joel] (cries out) Ow, my hip.

1302
00:52:19,067 --> 00:52:19,900
Your hip.

1303
00:52:21,067 --> 00:52:22,233
- [Tom] You can kill
them with a fork,

1304
00:52:22,233 --> 00:52:24,700
but please use a spoon.

1305
00:52:24,700 --> 00:52:27,633
- [Crow] It's the
Stone Wall Riots.

1306
00:52:30,000 --> 00:52:32,433
- [Joel] Fork all of ya.

1307
00:52:32,433 --> 00:52:33,767
- [Crow] Let go.

1308
00:52:37,233 --> 00:52:38,167
- [Tom] Ohp, probably shouldn't

1309
00:52:38,167 --> 00:52:40,667
have climbed on Sinbad's cape.

1310
00:52:42,533 --> 00:52:44,200
- Sinbad!
- I'm busy.

1311
00:52:46,967 --> 00:52:50,133
- [Tom] They paint
horses, don't they?

1312
00:52:52,133 --> 00:52:53,800
- [Crow] Hey, neigh means neigh.

1313
00:52:53,800 --> 00:52:55,067
- Help 'im get the horse there.

1314
00:52:55,067 --> 00:52:57,800
- [Barbarian] Get
that sail down.

1315
00:53:00,667 --> 00:53:02,133
- [Crow] Neigh,
what are you doing?

1316
00:53:02,133 --> 00:53:05,800
Dressing me up like I'm
Hoover or something?

1317
00:53:07,133 --> 00:53:08,533
- [Tom] Oh great.

1318
00:53:09,767 --> 00:53:11,400
(Crow laughs)

1319
00:53:11,400 --> 00:53:15,667
- [Joel] That guy's got the
wrong concept of a pony ride.

1320
00:53:15,667 --> 00:53:18,000
- [Crow] Whoo-hoo, your
hands cold, whoo-hoo.

1321
00:53:18,000 --> 00:53:20,200
- [Tom] Hey boss, I just
invented the Pony Express.

1322
00:53:20,200 --> 00:53:21,767
Get it?

1323
00:53:21,767 --> 00:53:26,067
- [Crow] Hey, I'm completely
capable of walking, thank you.

1324
00:53:26,067 --> 00:53:27,333
- [Tom] Hey fellas.

1325
00:53:27,333 --> 00:53:28,867
- [Joel] Did you see
that guy back there?

1326
00:53:28,867 --> 00:53:29,800
- [Crow] Looked pretty easy
but I don't know about that.

1327
00:53:29,800 --> 00:53:31,733
- [Joel] He's carrying a horse.

1328
00:53:36,200 --> 00:53:37,767
Jello tonight.
- No.

1329
00:53:40,400 --> 00:53:41,900
- You are the bravest
men I've ever known.

1330
00:53:41,900 --> 00:53:43,100
- [Tom] Thank you.

1331
00:53:43,100 --> 00:53:44,700
- We still must
search for the bird.

1332
00:53:44,700 --> 00:53:46,267
We can't let anything stop us.

1333
00:53:46,267 --> 00:53:49,233
- [Crow] Well, you're
certainly right, darling.

1334
00:53:49,233 --> 00:53:50,467
- [Tom] They did pretty good

1335
00:53:50,467 --> 00:53:53,733
for their first
season fight, huh?

1336
00:53:53,733 --> 00:53:56,600
(bird whistles)

1337
00:53:56,600 --> 00:53:58,133
- [Joel] Ah, it's
like glass out there.

1338
00:53:58,133 --> 00:54:00,133
I should be out water skiing.

1339
00:54:00,133 --> 00:54:02,833
(peaceful music)

1340
00:54:05,967 --> 00:54:06,800
- [Narrator] Due east--

1341
00:54:06,800 --> 00:54:08,233
- [Tom] Defeats Truman.

1342
00:54:08,233 --> 00:54:10,600
- [Narrator] The ships followed
the calls of exotic lands.

1343
00:54:10,600 --> 00:54:12,633
- [Crow] Hey, come over here.

1344
00:54:12,633 --> 00:54:14,833
- Rare spices--
- Rare.

1345
00:54:14,833 --> 00:54:17,867
- [Narrator] The crystal
palaces of Nashapur.

1346
00:54:17,867 --> 00:54:20,500
The many colored
gardens of Ababu.

1347
00:54:20,500 --> 00:54:22,633
The golden city of Bangalore.

1348
00:54:22,633 --> 00:54:27,033
- [Tom] The flint-colored
rocks of North Dacumbe.

1349
00:54:27,033 --> 00:54:28,767
- [Narrator] Until the
ships found themselves

1350
00:54:28,767 --> 00:54:31,533
on the coast of
mysterious India.

1351
00:54:32,767 --> 00:54:34,000
- [Crow] Hey, with
all those tents,

1352
00:54:34,000 --> 00:54:36,867
they could do a
Benny Hill sketch.

1353
00:54:36,867 --> 00:54:38,700
- [Joel] Hey, there's
George Harrison.

1354
00:54:38,700 --> 00:54:40,100
- [Tom] Yeah, hm.

1355
00:54:41,900 --> 00:54:43,833
Oh boy, this exotic
land is so different

1356
00:54:43,833 --> 00:54:46,500
from where we came from, oh boy.

1357
00:54:47,633 --> 00:54:49,667
- [Tom] Say, do you
have anything elephanty?

1358
00:54:49,667 --> 00:54:53,733
Sorta brassy-like trinkets
and stuff like that?

1359
00:54:53,733 --> 00:54:56,567
- [Joel] Hey, I'm
sacred, leave me alone.

1360
00:54:56,567 --> 00:54:58,800
- [Tom] It sure attracts lint.

1361
00:54:58,800 --> 00:55:00,233
- [Crow] Nobodies
gonna miss just one.

1362
00:55:00,233 --> 00:55:01,333
Come on, take it, easy.

1363
00:55:01,333 --> 00:55:03,833
It's just a banana, stay calm.

1364
00:55:05,133 --> 00:55:06,400
- [Tom] Come on, Polly.

1365
00:55:06,400 --> 00:55:08,733
Turn around and say
hello (bird squawk).

1366
00:55:08,733 --> 00:55:10,700
- [Joel] It's Rock
'em Sock 'Em Chickens.

1367
00:55:10,700 --> 00:55:14,100
(chickens cluck)

1368
00:55:14,100 --> 00:55:16,500
- Hey, look at the goods
from foreign lands here.

1369
00:55:16,500 --> 00:55:18,467
Rich goods, from foreign lands.

1370
00:55:18,467 --> 00:55:19,733
- [Tom] That's a
Junior Achievement.

1371
00:55:19,733 --> 00:55:22,267
- [Crow] No, he's not a
very skilled puppeteer.

1372
00:55:22,267 --> 00:55:24,167
- All of you, take a look
at what we have here.

1373
00:55:24,167 --> 00:55:25,667
- Take a look.

1374
00:55:25,667 --> 00:55:29,733
- [Tom] Oh man, these snakes
are all tangled up today.

1375
00:55:29,733 --> 00:55:33,900
- [Crow] That one goes
there (mumbles over snakes).

1376
00:55:33,900 --> 00:55:37,433
- [Tom] Where's that
Pronto Pup stand?

1377
00:55:37,433 --> 00:55:38,933
- Sinbad!

1378
00:55:38,933 --> 00:55:40,200
Sinbad!

1379
00:55:40,200 --> 00:55:43,167
- [Crow] You were great
in Necessary Roughness.

1380
00:55:43,167 --> 00:55:45,100
- I've discovered they
have a magic bird here,

1381
00:55:45,100 --> 00:55:46,733
which sings of happiness.

1382
00:55:46,733 --> 00:55:48,367
- I must see it at once.

1383
00:55:48,367 --> 00:55:51,367
- The Prince keeps it in a
golden tower behind seven walls.

1384
00:55:51,367 --> 00:55:52,300
- [Joel] Oh, they
shouldn't keep a bird

1385
00:55:52,300 --> 00:55:53,733
inside on such a nice day.

1386
00:55:53,733 --> 00:55:55,000
- No.
- Nuh-uh.

1387
00:55:55,000 --> 00:55:56,267
- There are a thousand
soldiers to guard it.

1388
00:55:56,267 --> 00:55:57,800
- I don't care.
- Careful, friend.

1389
00:55:57,800 --> 00:55:59,433
We must not rush into things.

1390
00:55:59,433 --> 00:56:01,067
This is a foreign place.

1391
00:56:01,067 --> 00:56:02,667
- But I must see this
bird at all cost.

1392
00:56:02,667 --> 00:56:05,500
- We must employ our
cunning here, Sinbad.

1393
00:56:05,500 --> 00:56:07,000
- [Tom] Watch Tripod rock.

1394
00:56:07,000 --> 00:56:09,533
- Their Prince loves good
steeds above all treasures.

1395
00:56:09,533 --> 00:56:11,567
Better than anything.

1396
00:56:11,567 --> 00:56:13,133
Do you understand me?

1397
00:56:13,133 --> 00:56:14,367
- [Crow] You're
gonna pull back a

1398
00:56:14,367 --> 00:56:15,733
bloody stump one of
these times, old man?

1399
00:56:15,733 --> 00:56:17,567
- Ah, that's wonderful.

1400
00:56:17,567 --> 00:56:19,533
(horns blow)

1401
00:56:19,533 --> 00:56:23,300
- [Tom] And now the
Aladdin proudly presents.

1402
00:56:25,467 --> 00:56:27,633
- [Crow] Please, spare
my trinket stand.

1403
00:56:27,633 --> 00:56:29,300
Oh, help me, please.

1404
00:56:33,100 --> 00:56:34,900
- [Joel] Hey,
suddenly it's after.

1405
00:56:34,900 --> 00:56:39,067
(all sing like Eastern
music instruments)

1406
00:56:41,567 --> 00:56:45,667
- [Tom] Ooh, ow, owie, chafe,
gotta get a case for thing.

1407
00:56:45,667 --> 00:56:46,667
- [Crow] Hm?

1408
00:56:47,867 --> 00:56:50,233
Well, this movie's
turned expensive.

1409
00:56:50,233 --> 00:56:54,167
(Tom sings along)
- See?

1410
00:56:54,167 --> 00:56:55,367
- [Tom] You know, you just

1411
00:56:55,367 --> 00:56:58,000
can't have too much
pageantry, huh?

1412
00:56:58,000 --> 00:57:00,667
(Tom hums along)

1413
00:57:00,667 --> 00:57:02,367
♪ Jumbo the Elephant

1414
00:57:02,367 --> 00:57:05,233
♪ Jumbo the Elephant and me

1415
00:57:05,233 --> 00:57:07,400
- Is it Kate Capshaw?
- No.

1416
00:57:12,400 --> 00:57:13,700
- [Tom] So what kind
of in-city mileage

1417
00:57:13,700 --> 00:57:15,133
do you think that
elephant gets here?

1418
00:57:15,133 --> 00:57:16,400
- [Joel] I know one
thing, they shouldn't have

1419
00:57:16,400 --> 00:57:17,833
come into the city
during rush hour.

1420
00:57:17,833 --> 00:57:19,533
That was a mistake.

1421
00:57:19,533 --> 00:57:21,567
- [Crow] It's the
Republican Convention.

1422
00:57:21,567 --> 00:57:24,867
Like with the elephant
and all the people and.

1423
00:57:24,867 --> 00:57:27,500
- [Joel] There's
the corn palace.

1424
00:57:27,500 --> 00:57:28,667
Leroy Neiman?

1425
00:57:28,667 --> 00:57:30,733
- Why do you not bow?

1426
00:57:30,733 --> 00:57:32,900
- We are free merchants,
from Copasand.

1427
00:57:32,900 --> 00:57:34,500
We come to sell our goods here.

1428
00:57:34,500 --> 00:57:36,300
Let me present
you with a sample,

1429
00:57:36,300 --> 00:57:38,133
- A sampo?
- As a gift.

1430
00:57:40,700 --> 00:57:43,133
- [Crow] I am not an animal.

1431
00:57:43,133 --> 00:57:45,033
Oh, I guess I am.

1432
00:57:45,033 --> 00:57:46,867
- Your horse?
- Oh yes.

1433
00:57:46,867 --> 00:57:48,133
- [Joel] Isn't is grand?

1434
00:57:48,133 --> 00:57:49,700
- What price will
you take for it?

1435
00:57:49,700 --> 00:57:51,333
- He is not for
sale, Your Highness.

1436
00:57:51,333 --> 00:57:52,500
Not to anyone.

1437
00:57:53,667 --> 00:57:56,767
- You surprise me that
you suffer me insolence.

1438
00:57:56,767 --> 00:57:59,567
- I cannot sell him,
and for that I regret.

1439
00:57:59,567 --> 00:58:02,400
But I might be talked into
trading him, if you like.

1440
00:58:02,400 --> 00:58:03,933
- [Tom] Negotiate anything.

1441
00:58:03,933 --> 00:58:05,167
- Why not?

1442
00:58:05,167 --> 00:58:06,167
State your trade.

1443
00:58:06,167 --> 00:58:08,567
- [Crow] Refrigerator repair.

1444
00:58:08,567 --> 00:58:10,533
- I hear that it
sings of happiness.

1445
00:58:10,533 --> 00:58:13,733
- [Tom] Yeah, well
you heard wrong.

1446
00:58:13,733 --> 00:58:15,833
- And that's what I
will take in trade.

1447
00:58:15,833 --> 00:58:17,567
- Impudent infidel.

1448
00:58:17,567 --> 00:58:19,667
Your presence here is insulting.

1449
00:58:19,667 --> 00:58:22,533
I shall have your fine
beast and your head.

1450
00:58:22,533 --> 00:58:24,700
The foot of my elephant
will crush you like a bug--

1451
00:58:24,700 --> 00:58:25,867
- [Tom] Give me five.

1452
00:58:25,867 --> 00:58:27,667
- And then the
horse will be mine.

1453
00:58:27,667 --> 00:58:28,700
- You cannot.

1454
00:58:28,700 --> 00:58:30,367
(Viewers cry out)

1455
00:58:30,367 --> 00:58:33,200
- [Crow] How's he doing that?

1456
00:58:33,200 --> 00:58:34,533
- See there?

1457
00:58:34,533 --> 00:58:36,533
This is a magic animal.

1458
00:58:36,533 --> 00:58:38,833
Whoever takes it away by force,

1459
00:58:38,833 --> 00:58:41,200
will be mortally
stricken immediately.

1460
00:58:41,200 --> 00:58:42,167
- Hmm.
- Oh dear.

1461
00:58:42,167 --> 00:58:43,400
Think of an offer.

1462
00:58:43,400 --> 00:58:44,300
- [Tom] He's not Sinbad.

1463
00:58:44,300 --> 00:58:46,000
Be careful, sweets.

1464
00:58:46,000 --> 00:58:48,100
- That's an excellent offer.

1465
00:58:48,100 --> 00:58:50,733
Let us play a game
of chess, merchant.

1466
00:58:50,733 --> 00:58:54,200
If you win, sir, the phoenix
of happiness is yours.

1467
00:58:54,200 --> 00:58:56,933
If not, the horse is mine.
- Okay.

1468
00:58:58,033 --> 00:59:00,767
- Well then, let's play.

1469
00:59:00,767 --> 00:59:02,933
- [Tom] You wanna?

1470
00:59:02,933 --> 00:59:05,367
(epic music)

1471
