- [Crow] Hey, look up there.

1715
01:09:07,133 --> 01:09:08,400
- What?
- Where?

1716
01:09:09,467 --> 01:09:11,667
I don't see it.
- No.

1717
01:09:11,667 --> 01:09:14,600
Oh, look, here comes the
world's slowest assault team.

1718
01:09:14,600 --> 01:09:15,967
- [Joel] Hey, Paul Wellstone,
right in the middle.

1719
01:09:15,967 --> 01:09:16,900
There he is.
- Whaddya know?

1720
01:09:16,900 --> 01:09:17,667
- What are we going to do?

1721
01:09:17,667 --> 01:09:18,900
- Be strong.

1722
01:09:18,900 --> 01:09:21,300
- Use your magic
bird to stop them.

1723
01:09:21,300 --> 01:09:22,233
- [Tom] Use your own magic bird.

1724
01:09:22,233 --> 01:09:23,900
- Sing your song, Phoenix.

1725
01:09:23,900 --> 01:09:26,233
Sing your song, wise bird.

1726
01:09:26,233 --> 01:09:27,900
And put them to sleep at once.

1727
01:09:27,900 --> 01:09:29,300
(Tom hacks and coughs)

1728
01:09:29,300 --> 01:09:30,533
- Go ahead, sing you--

1729
01:09:30,533 --> 01:09:32,300
- [Joel] Hey, watch the fin.

1730
01:09:32,300 --> 01:09:33,367
- Sing.
- Guy?

1731
01:09:35,633 --> 01:09:38,133
- Sing or I'll
pull them all out.

1732
01:09:38,133 --> 01:09:42,433
- [Tom] Oh, she fell
asleep on a cherry sucret.

1733
01:09:42,433 --> 01:09:44,367
- Hear my voice.

1734
01:09:44,367 --> 01:09:45,567
Forget all else.

1735
01:09:45,567 --> 01:09:47,433
- [Joel] Hey, she's
doing Marlena Dietrich.

1736
01:09:47,433 --> 01:09:50,133
- I know.
- Sleep deeply all men.

1737
01:09:50,133 --> 01:09:52,367
For sleep is the only true--

1738
01:09:52,367 --> 01:09:53,500
- This again.
- Hey, hey, wait.

1739
01:09:53,500 --> 01:09:54,900
Where's Crow?

1740
01:09:54,900 --> 01:09:55,733
- [Tom] I don't know.

1741
01:09:55,733 --> 01:09:56,567
Crow?

1742
01:09:57,733 --> 01:09:58,733
- [Joel] I don't
know where he is.

1743
01:09:58,733 --> 01:10:01,300
- My sweet song, peace--

1744
01:10:01,300 --> 01:10:04,133
- [Tom] Look, she's doing her
Garrison Keillor effect here.

1745
01:10:04,133 --> 01:10:05,200
Crow?

1746
01:10:05,200 --> 01:10:06,733
- Sleep.

1747
01:10:06,733 --> 01:10:09,600
- [Tom] Oh, next up, more of
that banjo and fiddle crap.

1748
01:10:09,600 --> 01:10:10,800
Coming up next.

1749
01:10:10,800 --> 01:10:11,967
- [Joel] We should go find Crow.

1750
01:10:11,967 --> 01:10:12,633
- You getting worried about--
- Yeah.

1751
01:10:12,633 --> 01:10:13,867
- [Tom] Crow?

1752
01:10:13,867 --> 01:10:14,600
- [Joel] I don't
see him anywhere.

1753
01:10:14,600 --> 01:10:15,533
- Crow?
- Crow?

1754
01:10:15,533 --> 01:10:18,700
(doors slide and slam shut)

1755
01:10:26,067 --> 01:10:28,000
- I couldn't find him anywhere.

1756
01:10:28,000 --> 01:10:29,633
- Ditto.

1757
01:10:29,633 --> 01:10:31,933
- Listen, did you check under
the control room stairwell?

1758
01:10:31,933 --> 01:10:33,600
Remember that one time he
took a bunch of cookies

1759
01:10:33,600 --> 01:10:35,833
and wedged himself under
there for about eight hours?

1760
01:10:35,833 --> 01:10:37,100
- No, he wasn't there, either.

1761
01:10:37,100 --> 01:10:39,533
But I found a Jolly
Rancher Firestick

1762
01:10:39,533 --> 01:10:40,967
with a little hair on it.

1763
01:10:40,967 --> 01:10:42,200
It had a really weird taste.

1764
01:10:42,200 --> 01:10:44,000
Kinda like Tabasco
sauce and Silly Putty.

1765
01:10:44,000 --> 01:10:45,167
I can't really recommend it.

1766
01:10:45,167 --> 01:10:46,200
- Tom, would you knock it off?

1767
01:10:46,200 --> 01:10:48,000
We're trying to find Crow.

1768
01:10:48,000 --> 01:10:50,567
- Maybe we should read
the note on the desk here.

1769
01:10:50,567 --> 01:10:54,567
- Okay, uh, guys, on
lifelong quest like Sinbad.

1770
01:10:56,433 --> 01:10:57,833
- He's not Sinbad.
- Tom?

1771
01:10:57,833 --> 01:10:59,267
- Sorry, sorry.

1772
01:10:59,267 --> 01:11:02,400
- Okay, guys, on lifelong
quest like Sinbad.

1773
01:11:02,400 --> 01:11:04,400
Shot myself out airlock.

1774
01:11:05,333 --> 01:11:07,200
Never returning.

1775
01:11:07,200 --> 01:11:09,100
Ham in fridge.

1776
01:11:09,100 --> 01:11:10,233
Crow.

1777
01:11:10,233 --> 01:11:11,700
- Huh.

1778
01:11:11,700 --> 01:11:13,600
- [Crow] Crow T. Robot
to Satellite of Love One.

1779
01:11:13,600 --> 01:11:15,267
Come in, Satellite of Love One.

1780
01:11:15,267 --> 01:11:16,467
- What? That's Crow.

1781
01:11:16,467 --> 01:11:17,767
The little fella must have taken

1782
01:11:17,767 --> 01:11:19,800
a communication
headset with him.

1783
01:11:19,800 --> 01:11:21,367
Come in, Crow.

1784
01:11:21,367 --> 01:11:23,267
- [Crow] Oh it's Joel, hi.

1785
01:11:23,267 --> 01:11:27,300
So, I took some
thrusters and shot myself

1786
01:11:27,300 --> 01:11:31,200
out the airlock to go on
my lifelong quest thingy.

1787
01:11:31,200 --> 01:11:33,633
It's not going real well.

1788
01:11:33,633 --> 01:11:36,667
Thrusters are out of
control, real cold,

1789
01:11:36,667 --> 01:11:40,500
and right now it seems as
though my doom is imminent.

1790
01:11:40,500 --> 01:11:41,767
So how are you?

1791
01:11:41,767 --> 01:11:43,967
- I'm fine, Crow,
but where are you?

1792
01:11:43,967 --> 01:11:45,433
- [Crow] I'm right
outside the ship.

1793
01:11:45,433 --> 01:11:47,733
- Get me rocket
number nine, quick.

1794
01:11:47,733 --> 01:11:50,833
- [Crow] Hi, I'll try
to fly past the window.

1795
01:11:50,833 --> 01:11:52,833
- There he goes.

1796
01:11:52,833 --> 01:11:54,100
- [Crow] Still haven't got

1797
01:11:54,100 --> 01:11:55,467
the hang of these
thruster things.

1798
01:11:55,467 --> 01:11:57,667
- Ah, Crow, this is Tom, hi.

1799
01:11:57,667 --> 01:11:59,567
If you're gonna die out
in the cold void of space,

1800
01:11:59,567 --> 01:12:02,267
can I have that Toblerone you've
been hiding under your bed?

1801
01:12:02,267 --> 01:12:03,800
- [Crow] Oh, I'm gonna die.

1802
01:12:03,800 --> 01:12:04,733
It's a given.

1803
01:12:04,733 --> 01:12:06,433
- Crow, you're not gonna die.

1804
01:12:06,433 --> 01:12:08,300
You just need to
slow yourself down

1805
01:12:08,300 --> 01:12:09,933
and get to one of the airlocks.

1806
01:12:09,933 --> 01:12:12,133
- [Crow] Slow myself
down (beep and crashing).

1807
01:12:12,133 --> 01:12:13,500
Owie, why do these
stupid antennae

1808
01:12:13,500 --> 01:12:14,933
have to stick out like this?

1809
01:12:14,933 --> 01:12:16,767
Oh, my hinder.

1810
01:12:16,767 --> 01:12:20,000
- Crow, I've got a feeling it's
just about commercial sign,

1811
01:12:20,000 --> 01:12:21,567
so we're gonna have to leave.

1812
01:12:21,567 --> 01:12:23,033
- [Crow] You guys go ahead.

1813
01:12:23,033 --> 01:12:24,633
I'm fine.

1814
01:12:24,633 --> 01:12:26,367
- There he goes.
- Whoa, there you are.

1815
01:12:26,367 --> 01:12:28,333
- Listen, Crow,
reverse your thrusters

1816
01:12:28,333 --> 01:12:30,800
and steer yourself back
to one of the airlocks.

1817
01:12:30,800 --> 01:12:33,867
On my way to theater, I'll
set them to external control.

1818
01:12:33,867 --> 01:12:36,133
- [Crow] Okay, sounds great.

1819
01:12:36,133 --> 01:12:37,067
I'm dead.

1820
01:12:37,067 --> 01:12:38,733
- We got a commercial sign here.

1821
01:12:38,733 --> 01:12:40,067
- He doesn't stand a chance.

1822
01:12:40,067 --> 01:12:41,167
We'll be right back.

1823
01:12:41,167 --> 01:12:44,067
(retro 80's music)

1824
01:12:48,067 --> 01:12:50,900
I can almost taste
that Toblerone.

1825
01:12:50,900 --> 01:12:54,967
- [Joel] Boy, I hope
Crow gets back in here.

1826
01:12:54,967 --> 01:12:56,400
- [Narrator] The great
wonders of the Earth.

1827
01:12:56,400 --> 01:12:58,200
(mechanical static)

1828
01:12:58,200 --> 01:13:00,900
(crashing and tumbling)

1829
01:13:00,900 --> 01:13:02,200
- [Joel] Golly.

1830
01:13:02,200 --> 01:13:03,800
Geez.

1831
01:13:03,800 --> 01:13:05,367
- [Crow] Came in
through the airlock.

1832
01:13:05,367 --> 01:13:06,367
Pretty easy.

1833
01:13:07,700 --> 01:13:09,200
- [Joel] Geez.

1834
01:13:09,200 --> 01:13:10,400
That was a close one.

1835
01:13:10,400 --> 01:13:11,600
- [Narrator] With
nothing but treachery

1836
01:13:11,600 --> 01:13:14,333
and futility as my reward.

1837
01:13:14,333 --> 01:13:16,467
And the Sphinx was verdant.

1838
01:13:16,467 --> 01:13:19,000
Find your happiness in Copasand.

1839
01:13:19,000 --> 01:13:20,833
- [Tom] You big loser.

1840
01:13:22,800 --> 01:13:24,700
- [Joel] Oh, he's holding
the remote control

1841
01:13:24,700 --> 01:13:27,067
for the slide projector.
- Oh!

1842
01:13:27,067 --> 01:13:30,667
- [Crow] Wait a minute,
I'm Sinbad, dammit.

1843
01:13:32,067 --> 01:13:34,300
- [Joel] Uh, Earth to Sinbad.

1844
01:13:34,300 --> 01:13:36,200
Hello, come in, Sinbad.

1845
01:13:38,533 --> 01:13:40,033
- [Tom] I'm a failure.

1846
01:13:40,033 --> 01:13:41,667
Lower than a weevil.

1847
01:13:41,667 --> 01:13:42,800
Next slide, please.

1848
01:13:42,800 --> 01:13:43,833
Thank you.

1849
01:13:43,833 --> 01:13:45,767
I'm feeling really bad.

1850
01:13:47,067 --> 01:13:50,900
- [Joel] I pledge
allegiance to the flag of--

1851
01:13:50,900 --> 01:13:52,200
- [Tom] Dorothy?

1852
01:13:52,200 --> 01:13:54,767
Dorothy, where are you?

1853
01:13:54,767 --> 01:13:56,100
- [Crow] Oh, hi.

1854
01:13:57,567 --> 01:13:58,867
- [Joel] What?

1855
01:13:58,867 --> 01:14:01,567
A big statue of George
Washington, the hell?

1856
01:14:01,567 --> 01:14:03,233
- It's the Sphinx.
- Oh.

1857
01:14:03,233 --> 01:14:05,233
- I must decide--

1858
01:14:05,233 --> 01:14:07,100
- [Crow] Hi, this is Dan Murray.

1859
01:14:07,100 --> 01:14:08,833
Welcome to Las Vegas.

1860
01:14:09,967 --> 01:14:12,000
- Hoist the sails for Copasand.

1861
01:14:12,000 --> 01:14:12,933
- [Tom] We can't.

1862
01:14:12,933 --> 01:14:14,433
We used them to wrap the horse.

1863
01:14:14,433 --> 01:14:16,400
- And return to our home.

1864
01:14:16,400 --> 01:14:17,400
- [Joel] Man, this
has been like waiting

1865
01:14:17,400 --> 01:14:19,733
for Gadeau on the high seas.

1866
01:14:21,400 --> 01:14:22,633
- [Crow] Those
sails were filthy.

1867
01:14:22,633 --> 01:14:24,933
It's good they sent 'em
out to be dry cleaned.

1868
01:14:24,933 --> 01:14:27,367
- [Tom] Hoist the
failure sails, mates.

1869
01:14:27,367 --> 01:14:28,900
We're going home.

1870
01:14:28,900 --> 01:14:30,667
♪ We're going home

1871
01:14:30,667 --> 01:14:33,033
♪ Our heads are bowed

1872
01:14:33,033 --> 01:14:34,300
♪ We failed

1873
01:14:34,300 --> 01:14:36,367
- [Tom] Boy, that
blew in quick, huh?

1874
01:14:36,367 --> 01:14:37,567
- [Joel] Kinda looks
like they sailed

1875
01:14:37,567 --> 01:14:40,567
right into the rinse cycle.

1876
01:14:40,567 --> 01:14:42,033
- [Crow] Hang on, Bucky.

1877
01:14:42,033 --> 01:14:43,300
Hang on, Bucky.

1878
01:14:44,533 --> 01:14:47,033
- [Tom] The Tidy
Bowl Races of 1993.

1879
01:14:47,033 --> 01:14:47,967
- [Crow] Look at the sails.

1880
01:14:47,967 --> 01:14:50,033
They're Mickey cake sails.

1881
01:14:53,100 --> 01:14:54,933
Look out, Mr. Maxwell!

1882
01:14:56,567 --> 01:14:57,933
- [Joel] I've glued
you all to the boats

1883
01:14:57,933 --> 01:15:01,433
and put rods into your
limbs for a reason.

1884
01:15:05,400 --> 01:15:07,333
(Tom coughs)

1885
01:15:07,333 --> 01:15:08,667
- Ohp, we lost one.
- Damn.

1886
01:15:08,667 --> 01:15:10,200
- [Tom] There goes another one.

1887
01:15:10,200 --> 01:15:14,967
- [Crow] Listen, why don't
we all take are furs off?

1888
01:15:14,967 --> 01:15:18,033
(Tom and Crow cough)

1889
01:15:19,333 --> 01:15:20,533
- [Joel] Wait a minute.

1890
01:15:20,533 --> 01:15:24,300
Pay toll ahead, 30 cents
per axle, what next?

1891
01:15:24,300 --> 01:15:25,133
(all gargle)

1892
01:15:25,133 --> 01:15:26,167
- [Tom] Don't worry.

1893
01:15:26,167 --> 01:15:28,033
This should burn off by noon.

1894
01:15:28,033 --> 01:15:29,533
- [Crow] Hey, we're
shooting the tube, man.

1895
01:15:29,533 --> 01:15:30,367
Wooo!

1896
01:15:36,833 --> 01:15:38,700
- [Joel] Well, we're
just gonna get wet now.

1897
01:15:38,700 --> 01:15:40,300
That's all there is to it.

1898
01:15:40,300 --> 01:15:41,867
- I have failed you, my friends.

1899
01:15:41,867 --> 01:15:43,633
I had forgotten
about King Neptune,

1900
01:15:43,633 --> 01:15:45,467
and did not make him an
offering as I should.

1901
01:15:45,467 --> 01:15:46,800
- [Tom] Oh yeah.

1902
01:15:48,000 --> 01:15:49,600
- I know something
will satisfy him.

1903
01:15:49,600 --> 01:15:51,433
There must be a human sacrifice.

1904
01:15:51,433 --> 01:15:55,133
- [Tom] Why is
everybody lookin' at me?

1905
01:15:55,133 --> 01:15:56,667
- I led you here.

1906
01:15:56,667 --> 01:15:59,400
And if there is to be a
sacrifice, it shall be me.

1907
01:15:59,400 --> 01:16:02,433
(Viewers cheer)

1908
01:16:02,433 --> 01:16:03,833
- We shall draw lots for this.

1909
01:16:03,833 --> 01:16:05,500
- That we shall, Sinbad.

1910
01:16:05,500 --> 01:16:06,967
We are all brothers
and so must share

1911
01:16:06,967 --> 01:16:09,933
the good things and the bad.
(all agree)

1912
01:16:09,933 --> 01:16:11,367
- Wait a minute, friends--

1913
01:16:11,367 --> 01:16:12,767
- [Crow] I'll bring Neptune
out in just a minute.

1914
01:16:12,767 --> 01:16:14,867
- I am heavily
indebted to Neptune

1915
01:16:14,867 --> 01:16:16,533
so I shall go into the sea.

1916
01:16:16,533 --> 01:16:18,633
- [Joel] Okay, fine.

1917
01:16:18,633 --> 01:16:20,967
- I have one last favor to--
- Nope, nope.

1918
01:16:20,967 --> 01:16:22,233
No time for that, in you go.

1919
01:16:22,233 --> 01:16:24,500
- Throw a cypress boat
onto the water for me.

1920
01:16:24,500 --> 01:16:27,800
And give me my harp
to take with me.

1921
01:16:27,800 --> 01:16:32,233
- [Crow] No, don't let
him take the harp, please.

1922
01:16:32,233 --> 01:16:33,467
- Do not cry now, Abidad.

1923
01:16:33,467 --> 01:16:35,000
- [Tom] I'm not
crying, my face is wet.

1924
01:16:35,000 --> 01:16:37,833
- Another time, and you
shall be a man then.

1925
01:16:37,833 --> 01:16:38,800
- [Joel] Yeah, right, whatever.

1926
01:16:38,800 --> 01:16:40,033
You wanna hop in, Sinbad?

1927
01:16:40,033 --> 01:16:42,633
It's getting bad out here.

1928
01:16:42,633 --> 01:16:43,567
- [Crow] We lost two guys.

1929
01:16:43,567 --> 01:16:45,067
You don't have to go now.

1930
01:16:45,067 --> 01:16:47,200
- Remember me to Lubiria, and
the good people of Copasand.

1931
01:16:47,200 --> 01:16:49,633
- [Joel] Goodbye, Sinbad.

1932
01:16:49,633 --> 01:16:52,500
- [Tom] Think you're
missing your wave.

1933
01:16:52,500 --> 01:16:53,433
There it goes.

1934
01:16:53,433 --> 01:16:54,833
- I am coming to you, Neptune.

1935
01:16:54,833 --> 01:16:57,233
- [Joel] No, wait, stop, don't.

1936
01:16:57,233 --> 01:16:59,133
- [Crow] Make sure he's not
holding onto a rope or anything.

1937
01:16:59,133 --> 01:17:00,167
- [Tom] Whack him with an oar.

1938
01:17:00,167 --> 01:17:02,267
- [Crow] Is that his hand?

1939
01:17:04,033 --> 01:17:05,867
(Tom gargles)

1940
01:17:05,867 --> 01:17:06,867
- [Joel] There he is now.

1941
01:17:06,867 --> 01:17:08,800
He's standing on
an air mattress.

1942
01:17:08,800 --> 01:17:11,300
(Tom gargles)

1943
01:17:15,200 --> 01:17:16,800
- [Crow] Might try
getting under the water.

1944
01:17:16,800 --> 01:17:18,633
Works better that way.

1945
01:17:21,200 --> 01:17:23,300
- [Joel] I'll be going
down in a minute, honestly.

1946
01:17:23,300 --> 01:17:24,900
I'll be right down.

1947
01:17:26,967 --> 01:17:31,133
- [Crow] Sinbad, old boy,
you're out too far, man.

1948
01:17:33,467 --> 01:17:35,933
- [Joel] Yeah, thanks for
sacrificing yourself, Sinbad.

1949
01:17:35,933 --> 01:17:37,667
(gargles)

1950
01:17:37,667 --> 01:17:40,833
- [Tom] We will
return to The Tempest.

1951
01:17:41,800 --> 01:17:45,100
(vocalized motorboat)

1952
01:17:45,100 --> 01:17:50,033
- [Crow] Hey, I'm actually
making pretty good time here.

1953
01:17:50,033 --> 01:17:52,267
(gargling)

1954
01:17:53,900 --> 01:17:54,900
- Well.
- Hm.

1955
01:17:57,033 --> 01:17:59,200
- [Crow] Hello, breakfast.

1956
01:18:02,500 --> 01:18:03,900
- [Tom] Which way
did she say again?

1957
01:18:03,900 --> 01:18:06,333
Oh, what the heck
did she say again?

1958
01:18:06,333 --> 01:18:07,833
I'll just wing it.

1959
01:18:08,733 --> 01:18:11,967
- [Narrator] Down, down, down--

1960
01:18:11,967 --> 01:18:13,400
- [Crow] Rock lobster.

1961
01:18:13,400 --> 01:18:16,500
- [Narrator] There, before
his astonished eyes,

1962
01:18:16,500 --> 01:18:18,933
was the miraculous
kingdom of Neptune.

1963
01:18:18,933 --> 01:18:21,867
- [Tom] And the
capital of Neptuneburg.

1964
01:18:21,867 --> 01:18:23,067
- [Narrator] Which revealed the

1965
01:18:23,067 --> 01:18:26,700
splendor of the magical
city below the sea.

1966
01:18:26,700 --> 01:18:28,900
- [Joel] You don't have
a wet dry vac, do ya?

1967
01:18:28,900 --> 01:18:31,333
- Precious than I am on land?

1968
01:18:31,333 --> 01:18:33,467
- And I say iron
is more precious.

1969
01:18:33,467 --> 01:18:36,300
- Not so.
- I say it is so.

1970
01:18:36,300 --> 01:18:39,267
- Not so and how dare you--
- Scuse me?

1971
01:18:39,267 --> 01:18:40,433
- [Tom] Mr. And Mrs. Neptune.

1972
01:18:40,433 --> 01:18:43,133
- I am king.
I rule everything.

1973
01:18:43,133 --> 01:18:46,067
- I rule here also, and you
must obey me if you want

1974
01:18:46,067 --> 01:18:48,667
peace here in this kingdom
without any trouble from me.

1975
01:18:48,667 --> 01:18:50,367
- I am ruler.
- I also.

1976
01:18:50,367 --> 01:18:53,067
- I am ruler and you
will do what I tell you,

1977
01:18:53,067 --> 01:18:55,300
or I will send you
back to your Mother.

1978
01:18:55,300 --> 01:18:58,700
- [Crow] I remember
this routine from radio.

1979
01:18:58,700 --> 01:19:00,633
- [Joel] Sting is here.

1980
01:19:02,033 --> 01:19:03,733
- We have been waiting for you.

1981
01:19:03,733 --> 01:19:06,067
- [Crow] How come water
isn't wet underwater?

1982
01:19:06,067 --> 01:19:08,100
- I have it here with me, sire.

1983
01:19:08,100 --> 01:19:09,900
- Well then play.

1984
01:19:09,900 --> 01:19:12,100
- He looks a great deal
like my cousin, Dermra.

1985
01:19:12,100 --> 01:19:13,567
- How can you say that?

1986
01:19:13,567 --> 01:19:15,200
He looks nothing like
Dermra, just look at him.

1987
01:19:15,200 --> 01:19:16,800
- Dermra.
- Just look at him.

1988
01:19:16,800 --> 01:19:18,033
- Dermra.

1989
01:19:18,033 --> 01:19:19,267
- Will you stop
arguing with me--

1990
01:19:19,267 --> 01:19:20,533
- [Crow] Don't talk
about the boy, Martha.

1991
01:19:20,533 --> 01:19:21,700
- Dermra!

1992
01:19:21,700 --> 01:19:22,633
- Tell her you
look nothing at all

1993
01:19:22,633 --> 01:19:24,333
like her stupid cousin, Dermra.

1994
01:19:24,333 --> 01:19:25,600
- He's not stupid.

1995
01:19:25,600 --> 01:19:26,967
- Allow me, sire,
to play some music

1996
01:19:26,967 --> 01:19:27,967
for you and for the Queen.

1997
01:19:27,967 --> 01:19:29,200
- [Joel] So you'll shut up.

1998
01:19:29,200 --> 01:19:31,900
- Something that
might cheer me up.

1999
01:19:32,933 --> 01:19:35,367
(harp music)

2000
01:19:36,567 --> 01:19:40,467
♪ Let's start at
the very beginning

2001
01:19:41,433 --> 01:19:43,267
- [Joel] David Crosby?

2002
01:19:45,400 --> 01:19:46,900
- [Crow] Sir, sir,
we're underwater

2003
01:19:46,900 --> 01:19:49,633
but we still have standards.

2004
01:19:49,633 --> 01:19:51,033
- [Joel] Hey, he put a
quarter in the throne

2005
01:19:51,033 --> 01:19:52,733
and now he gets to ride it.

2006
01:19:52,733 --> 01:19:54,867
- Get away from me, silly cat.

2007
01:19:54,867 --> 01:19:56,400
- [Tom] Kill me.

2008
01:19:56,400 --> 01:19:57,233
Kill me.

2009
01:19:58,367 --> 01:19:59,267
Kill me, kill me.

2010
01:19:59,267 --> 01:20:01,200
Please God, kill me.

2011
01:20:01,200 --> 01:20:02,433
- [Crow] Go ahead.

2012
01:20:02,433 --> 01:20:05,200
Play something that
might cheer me up.

2013
01:20:06,433 --> 01:20:07,633
- [Joel] Drink up, everyone.

2014
01:20:07,633 --> 01:20:10,667
Club Octopi will be
closing in five minutes.

2015
01:20:10,667 --> 01:20:13,900
- [Tom] It's the Ice
Capades with Jill Trenary.

2016
01:20:13,900 --> 01:20:17,700
- [Crow] Ah, sir,
I really should be
getting back to my men.

2017
01:20:17,700 --> 01:20:19,067
- [Joel] You know
that ceiling octopus

2018
01:20:19,067 --> 01:20:21,900
really helps with
the circulation.

2019
01:20:24,967 --> 01:20:28,267
- [Tom] You know I kinda wish
they'd celebrate internally.

2020
01:20:28,267 --> 01:20:31,167
- [Crow] Is this supposed
to be Sinbad's stomach?

2021
01:20:31,167 --> 01:20:32,667
- [Tom] Are you humming?

2022
01:20:32,667 --> 01:20:33,867
- [Joel] Is there a
phone I could use?

2023
01:20:33,867 --> 01:20:35,333
I just have to
make a quick call.

2024
01:20:35,333 --> 01:20:37,767
- Faster, Sinbad, faster.

2025
01:20:37,767 --> 01:20:40,433
- [Crow] Do you know any
Rimsky Korsakov cause he--

2026
01:20:40,433 --> 01:20:44,300
- [Tom] Bugs me the way
he's playing that thing.

2027
01:20:44,300 --> 01:20:47,233
(retro 80's music)

2028
01:20:50,167 --> 01:20:52,600
(epic music)

2029
01:20:55,500 --> 01:20:59,667
- [Joel] Hey, that sacrifice
is really working out, Sinbad.

2030
01:21:01,100 --> 01:21:03,233
- [Crow] Stroke, stroke, stroke,

2031
01:21:03,233 --> 01:21:07,233
drown, drown, drown (gargling).

2032
01:21:11,133 --> 01:21:12,833
- [Joel] Now wait a
minute, how does that work?

2033
01:21:12,833 --> 01:21:14,867
- [Crow] I'm trying
to play, do you mind?

2034
01:21:14,867 --> 01:21:16,367
- Ships been wrecked?

2035
01:21:16,367 --> 01:21:17,633
Crews been drowned?

2036
01:21:17,633 --> 01:21:20,533
- [Tom] Grandpa
fell down the well?

2037
01:21:23,067 --> 01:21:24,300
- [Neptune] What just happened?

2038
01:21:24,300 --> 01:21:25,900
- [Joel] I'm gonna
save you for later.

2039
01:21:25,900 --> 01:21:27,467
You stopped the music.

2040
01:21:27,467 --> 01:21:29,067
- My harp string, sire.

2041
01:21:29,067 --> 01:21:30,733
- [Crow] The salt water
messed up the tuning.

2042
01:21:30,733 --> 01:21:34,267
- I must return to the earth
in order to get new ones.

2043
01:21:34,267 --> 01:21:38,033
(Neptune awws and Tom mocks)

2044
01:21:38,033 --> 01:21:39,833
- He'll go back
to earth and, and

2045
01:21:39,833 --> 01:21:41,567
he'll never come back again.

2046
01:21:41,567 --> 01:21:43,000
- Yes.

2047
01:21:43,000 --> 01:21:46,067
To insure your return, you
must marry one of my daughters.

2048
01:21:46,067 --> 01:21:47,533
- [Tom] Or leave your license.

2049
01:21:47,533 --> 01:21:49,100
- [Neptune] Are
they not beautiful?

2050
01:21:49,100 --> 01:21:50,367
- [Queen] Anyone would be lucky

2051
01:21:50,367 --> 01:21:52,600
to have you for a
husband, Sinbad.

2052
01:21:52,600 --> 01:21:53,833
- Pick one.

2053
01:21:53,833 --> 01:21:57,267
Pick the one you like
the best, my son.

2054
01:21:57,267 --> 01:21:58,667
- [Tom] Daughter
number one wears

2055
01:21:58,667 --> 01:22:01,800
a star on her head and
is fond of grouper.

2056
01:22:01,800 --> 01:22:03,500
- [Crow] Number two, if I
came home late one night,

2057
01:22:03,500 --> 01:22:05,100
what would you say?

2058
01:22:06,267 --> 01:22:08,100
- Tell Father that I
am the one you choose.

2059
01:22:08,100 --> 01:22:11,367
- [Joel] I'm not gonna
choose the infant of Prague.

2060
01:22:11,367 --> 01:22:12,800
- But I cannot marry you.

2061
01:22:12,800 --> 01:22:14,233
- I know all about your Lubiria.

2062
01:22:14,233 --> 01:22:15,200
- [Crow] Hey, that cleared up.

2063
01:22:15,200 --> 01:22:17,100
- I will help you once more.

2064
01:22:17,100 --> 01:22:18,933
- [Tom] He's got a nice
embouchure, doesn't he?

2065
01:22:18,933 --> 01:22:19,933
- Here is my choice.

2066
01:22:19,933 --> 01:22:21,233
- You don't want that one.

2067
01:22:21,233 --> 01:22:23,067
She's the favorite
of all my children.

2068
01:22:23,067 --> 01:22:24,500
Pick another.

2069
01:22:24,500 --> 01:22:26,533
- No, only this one.

2070
01:22:26,533 --> 01:22:27,900
- How dare you speak
to me like that?

2071
01:22:27,900 --> 01:22:30,167
You are only a guest
in this kingdom,

2072
01:22:30,167 --> 01:22:31,367
and you shall do
as I tell you or

2073
01:22:31,367 --> 01:22:33,100
you will not live to rights.

2074
01:22:33,100 --> 01:22:34,533
- Try Mother now.

2075
01:22:35,700 --> 01:22:37,533
- [Tom] Poopy, please.

2076
01:22:38,667 --> 01:22:41,933
- Now wasn't I
offered my choice?

2077
01:22:41,933 --> 01:22:43,433
- But you shall
have your choice.

2078
01:22:43,433 --> 01:22:45,667
- And I say he will
not marry Morgiana.

2079
01:22:45,667 --> 01:22:48,900
- And I say he shall.
- And I say he won't.

2080
01:22:48,900 --> 01:22:51,000
- He shall or you'll regret it.

2081
01:22:51,000 --> 01:22:53,667
- [Crow] You knuckleknobs.

2082
01:22:53,667 --> 01:22:56,767
- I do not care (sobs).

2083
01:22:56,767 --> 01:22:59,067
- [Joel] Boy, they
started early today.

2084
01:22:59,067 --> 01:22:59,900
Weird.

2085
01:23:02,700 --> 01:23:06,100
- [Tom] Here, quickly, follow
me down the fallopian tube.

2086
01:23:06,100 --> 01:23:08,167
- [Joel] Boy, now she's
got so much planning to do.

2087
01:23:08,167 --> 01:23:11,800
She's got to register,
pick out a bridesmaid.

2088
01:23:11,800 --> 01:23:15,100
- [Crow] You want
a carrot, Sinbad?

2089
01:23:15,100 --> 01:23:17,000
- [Joel] This started getting
weird a little while ago,

2090
01:23:17,000 --> 01:23:18,667
didn't it?
- Yup yup.

2091
01:23:21,533 --> 01:23:23,633
- I cannot marry you,
oh lovely princess.

2092
01:23:23,633 --> 01:23:24,567
- [Crow] I have Lubiria.

2093
01:23:24,567 --> 01:23:25,833
- You must know that I can't.

2094
01:23:25,833 --> 01:23:26,867
- [Crow] It's eating
onto my embouchure.

2095
01:23:26,867 --> 01:23:29,667
- Please stop worrying, Sinbad.

2096
01:23:29,667 --> 01:23:32,167
Your freedom is
going to be spared.

2097
01:23:32,167 --> 01:23:33,533
- I love her very much indeed.

2098
01:23:33,533 --> 01:23:36,033
- I know.
- With all my heart.

2099
01:23:36,033 --> 01:23:37,500
- [Joel] I understand
completely.

2100
01:23:37,500 --> 01:23:38,433
- Forgive me for this.

2101
01:23:38,433 --> 01:23:39,233
- [Joel] Hey, no problem here.

2102
01:23:39,233 --> 01:23:40,067
- It must be.

2103
01:23:40,067 --> 01:23:40,900
- [Joel] Well, beat it.

2104
01:23:40,900 --> 01:23:42,667
- Fate willed it so.

2105
01:23:42,667 --> 01:23:45,033
- [Crow] Hey, there's
plenty of fish in the sea.

2106
01:23:45,033 --> 01:23:47,933
- Very much.
- Yes, with all my heart.

2107
01:23:47,933 --> 01:23:48,967
- [Joel] And part of my spleen,

2108
01:23:48,967 --> 01:23:50,200
and a little bit of my liver.

2109
01:23:50,200 --> 01:23:53,267
- I cannot be angry with
you for this refusal.

2110
01:23:53,267 --> 01:23:54,467
- [Crow] So goodbye.

2111
01:23:54,467 --> 01:23:57,900
- You are very
proud of your love.

2112
01:23:57,900 --> 01:23:59,067
It is a wonderful thing.

2113
01:23:59,067 --> 01:24:00,967
- [Tom] To see you leave.

2114
01:24:00,967 --> 01:24:03,567
- So what can I do to help you?

2115
01:24:03,567 --> 01:24:05,367
- You have helped
me so much already.

2116
01:24:05,367 --> 01:24:06,533
- [Joel] Do you validate?

2117
01:24:06,533 --> 01:24:07,467
- [Crow] Welp, gotta go.

2118
01:24:07,467 --> 01:24:09,267
- But there is one more favor.

2119
01:24:09,267 --> 01:24:10,600
If I could get back to land--

2120
01:24:10,600 --> 01:24:13,767
- [Tom] And I've
always wanted a pony.

2121
01:24:15,200 --> 01:24:16,600
- Alright, my friend.

2122
01:24:16,600 --> 01:24:18,000
- [Joel] And could you
introduce me to Darryl Hannah?

2123
01:24:18,000 --> 01:24:19,100
- I will try.

2124
01:24:20,133 --> 01:24:22,500
- He's taken away my favorite.

2125
01:24:22,500 --> 01:24:24,100
My favorite little daughter.

2126
01:24:24,100 --> 01:24:26,767
- [Crow] Gotta go
sleep with Luca Brazi.

2127
01:24:26,767 --> 01:24:29,500
- [Tom] Somebody
pulled my tail (cries).

2128
01:24:29,500 --> 01:24:30,733
- Make haste, Sinbad,

2129
01:24:30,733 --> 01:24:32,933
and stop for nothing
until you reach home.

2130
01:24:32,933 --> 01:24:37,267
- [Joel] Man, I've done some
weird things before but wow.

2131
01:24:37,267 --> 01:24:39,300
- I shall never see
you again, Sinbad.

2132
01:24:39,300 --> 01:24:41,067
- I shall bless
you in my prayers.

2133
01:24:41,067 --> 01:24:44,600
♪ Marble the Mustang

2134
01:24:44,600 --> 01:24:48,033
- [Tom] How do you
work this thing?

2135
01:24:48,033 --> 01:24:52,067
- [Joel] There goes
a stupid, stupid man.

2136
01:24:52,067 --> 01:24:55,667
- [Crow] It's
unforgiven underwater.

2137
01:24:55,667 --> 01:24:57,467
- He's running away.
- Huh?

2138
01:24:57,467 --> 01:24:59,700
- Sinbad's escaped.
- I'm drunk.

2139
01:24:59,700 --> 01:25:01,300
- Sinbad's escaped?

2140
01:25:02,333 --> 01:25:03,900
Get me my chariot.

2141
01:25:03,900 --> 01:25:05,167
I'll catch the scoundrel.

2142
01:25:05,167 --> 01:25:07,500
- [Tom] Doh, I did it again.

2143
01:25:09,433 --> 01:25:12,667
- [Joel] Oh man, it's
a team of prawns.

2144
01:25:16,033 --> 01:25:17,467
- [Crow] Boy, he's really
hugging this seahorse.

2145
01:25:17,467 --> 01:25:19,133
- [Tom] Ease up, buddy.

2146
01:25:19,133 --> 01:25:21,933
I got an exoskeleton,
for crying out loud.

2147
01:25:21,933 --> 01:25:24,700
- [Crow]
Duh-duh-duh-duh-duh-duh,
Atlantis.

2148
01:25:24,700 --> 01:25:27,133
Cause it's underwater.
- Yeah.

2149
01:25:29,100 --> 01:25:29,933
- [Joel] Fly, monkeys!

2150
01:25:29,933 --> 01:25:31,600
Oh I mean, seahorse.

2151
01:25:36,100 --> 01:25:38,933
- [Tom] This didn't
really happen.

2152
01:25:42,167 --> 01:25:44,167
- [Crow] Leave me alone.

2153
01:25:45,333 --> 01:25:48,100
(dramatic music)

2154
01:25:52,900 --> 01:25:55,033
- [Joel] (gargles) You
want me to wait, pal?

2155
01:25:55,033 --> 01:25:57,600
- [Crow] That's okay.

2156
01:25:57,600 --> 01:25:59,900
- [Tom] Hey, I won.

2157
01:25:59,900 --> 01:26:02,767
- [Joel] He's kissing a gopher.

2158
01:26:02,767 --> 01:26:05,200
- [Crow] She's been standing
there for six years.

2159
01:26:05,200 --> 01:26:06,333
- [Tom] Whoa,
gotta go, gotta go.

2160
01:26:06,333 --> 01:26:07,933
Really bad.

2161
01:26:07,933 --> 01:26:11,000
All that water and gotta go.

2162
01:26:11,000 --> 01:26:11,933
- Lubiria?

2163
01:26:11,933 --> 01:26:14,533
- [Joel] And it's treatable.

2164
01:26:14,533 --> 01:26:16,233
- I have returned.

2165
01:26:16,233 --> 01:26:20,400
- [Crow] Nothing happened
between me and the sea babe.

2166
01:26:22,033 --> 01:26:23,667
♪ Here we come back

2167
01:26:23,667 --> 01:26:25,267
Look at that, he's
there already.

2168
01:26:25,267 --> 01:26:26,867
We left before him.

2169
01:26:28,767 --> 01:26:31,100
- [Crow] Sinbad's back, day off!

2170
01:26:31,100 --> 01:26:33,700
- Come on.
- We're off again.

2171
01:26:33,700 --> 01:26:35,900
- Hey, guess who's back?
- Stop working, everybody.

2172
01:26:35,900 --> 01:26:39,433
It's him.
- Day off, Sinbad again.

2173
01:26:39,433 --> 01:26:42,233
Let's go.
Down to the docks.

2174
01:26:42,233 --> 01:26:46,367
For crying out loud,
I can't believe this.

2175
01:26:46,367 --> 01:26:50,100
- [Joel] Well, they got
the failure sails up.

2176
01:26:52,500 --> 01:26:53,400
- [Crow] Go away.

2177
01:26:53,400 --> 01:26:55,500
Big plague here.
Go away.

2178
01:26:55,500 --> 01:26:56,933
Death and stuff.

2179
01:26:56,933 --> 01:27:00,167
- [Joel] Oh, the merchants
are acting up again.

2180
01:27:00,167 --> 01:27:03,067
♪ We're gonna make it after all

2181
01:27:03,067 --> 01:27:04,000
- [Tom] So, Sinbad,
how 'bout that

2182
01:27:04,000 --> 01:27:06,233
bluebird of happiness, huh?

2183
01:27:07,733 --> 01:27:09,000
- [Villager] Where is Sinbad?

2184
01:27:09,000 --> 01:27:12,100
- [Joel] Now where's Waldo?
There he is.

2185
01:27:12,967 --> 01:27:14,300
- He is no more.

2186
01:27:17,233 --> 01:27:19,067
- Here I am, my friends.

2187
01:27:19,067 --> 01:27:20,233
I have returned to you.

2188
01:27:20,233 --> 01:27:22,067
(Viewers boo)

2189
01:27:22,067 --> 01:27:24,900
- [Crow] This guy's
like a bad penny.

2190
01:27:24,900 --> 01:27:26,200
- [Tom] Get 'im
guys, tear him up.

2191
01:27:26,200 --> 01:27:28,800
(crowd cheers)

2192
01:27:31,233 --> 01:27:32,167
Everybody--

2193
01:27:32,167 --> 01:27:34,033
♪ Welcome the failures

2194
01:27:34,033 --> 01:27:38,267
♪ They have failed again

2195
01:27:38,267 --> 01:27:40,300
- Did you find the
bird of happiness?

2196
01:27:40,300 --> 01:27:41,700
- There is no bird.

2197
01:27:41,700 --> 01:27:43,300
- Then where is happiness?

2198
01:27:43,300 --> 01:27:45,600
- Here, it's been here always.

2199
01:27:45,600 --> 01:27:48,067
- [Joel] Oh, bogus,
everybody go back home.

2200
01:27:48,067 --> 01:27:49,800
- Our ships have been
around the world--

2201
01:27:49,800 --> 01:27:51,033
- [Joel] Oh great.

2202
01:27:51,033 --> 01:27:52,267
- We've seen amazing
and marvelous things.

2203
01:27:52,267 --> 01:27:54,367
- [Crow] You went
to the Quad-Cities.

2204
01:27:54,367 --> 01:27:57,000
- To compare with our own home.

2205
01:27:57,000 --> 01:27:57,967
(Viewers start)

2206
01:27:57,967 --> 01:27:59,133
- [Joel] Let's get out of here.

2207
01:27:59,133 --> 01:28:00,333
- Follow your
hearts to happiness.

2208
01:28:00,333 --> 01:28:02,900
- [Joel] Stop
looking into my soul.

2209
01:28:02,900 --> 01:28:04,100
- [Crow] Hey, what about me?

2210
01:28:04,100 --> 01:28:05,033
What's going on?

2211
01:28:05,033 --> 01:28:05,967
Where am I?

2212
01:28:07,433 --> 01:28:11,200
(doors sliding and slamming)

2213
01:28:16,733 --> 01:28:19,767
- Hey, look who's decided
to visit the ship today.

2214
01:28:19,767 --> 01:28:22,067
It's the lovable,
huggable channel cat

2215
01:28:22,067 --> 01:28:25,233
from the underwater scenes
in this week's Sinbad movie.

2216
01:28:25,233 --> 01:28:26,400
- That wasn't Sinbad.

2217
01:28:26,400 --> 01:28:28,133
- Wow, is that ever boss.

2218
01:28:28,133 --> 01:28:31,133
- I'm really happy
to be here, Crow.

2219
01:28:32,033 --> 01:28:33,333
- It knows my name.

2220
01:28:33,333 --> 01:28:34,533
Wait a minute.

2221
01:28:34,533 --> 01:28:36,367
- And how's Tom Servo?

2222
01:28:37,933 --> 01:28:40,600
- Fine, thanks for
asking, Channel Ca--

2223
01:28:40,600 --> 01:28:41,833
wait a minute.

2224
01:28:41,833 --> 01:28:43,067
You're not the same fish
from the Sinbad movie.

2225
01:28:43,067 --> 01:28:44,633
- That wasn't Sinbad.

2226
01:28:44,633 --> 01:28:46,133
- Are you thinking
what I'm thinking?

2227
01:28:46,133 --> 01:28:48,567
- Yep yep yep, there's no way
that fish is from the movie.

2228
01:28:48,567 --> 01:28:49,767
He's doing something.

2229
01:28:49,767 --> 01:28:51,433
- Yeah, I hear you big time.

2230
01:28:51,433 --> 01:28:54,733
That thing's no more
alive than I am.

2231
01:28:54,733 --> 01:28:56,267
What's it made out of?

2232
01:28:56,267 --> 01:28:58,200
If I had to guess
I'd say some sort of

2233
01:28:58,200 --> 01:29:01,000
aluminum armature with
a webbing of pneumatics,

2234
01:29:01,000 --> 01:29:02,667
but still I don't
see any tubes off it

2235
01:29:02,667 --> 01:29:03,500
or a compressor anywhere.

2236
01:29:03,500 --> 01:29:04,967
- No no no, Crow.

2237
01:29:04,967 --> 01:29:06,300
Just look at the action he's
getting with that thing.

2238
01:29:06,300 --> 01:29:08,500
It's definitely not
audio animatronics.

2239
01:29:08,500 --> 01:29:10,833
Now if my guess is
right, and it usually is,

2240
01:29:10,833 --> 01:29:13,000
I bet my wife that
Joel rotosculpted

2241
01:29:13,000 --> 01:29:15,067
the fish from the movie,
digitized and copied

2242
01:29:15,067 --> 01:29:16,933
extra frames of
the mouth movement,

2243
01:29:16,933 --> 01:29:18,733
and then simply used a
laser projector to mat

2244
01:29:18,733 --> 01:29:20,233
the fish footage over his hand.

2245
01:29:20,233 --> 01:29:22,367
Then there's just a small
matter of adding the voice,

2246
01:29:22,367 --> 01:29:23,833
which he's obviously
doing himself.

2247
01:29:23,833 --> 01:29:25,433
- No, no way, I'm
definitely seeing and

2248
01:29:25,433 --> 01:29:28,233
rendering this thing
in three dimensions.

2249
01:29:28,233 --> 01:29:29,700
Nope, sorry, Tommy.

2250
01:29:29,700 --> 01:29:32,400
- Ah, geez, Crow, it defies
any kind of explanation.

2251
01:29:32,400 --> 01:29:33,900
- Oh, look at that thing.

2252
01:29:33,900 --> 01:29:35,600
Those eyes, weird, huh?

2253
01:29:35,600 --> 01:29:39,500
- Hey, how's Tom--
(Crow starts)

2254
01:29:39,500 --> 01:29:42,767
And Crow?
- It knows what I'm thinking.

2255
01:29:42,767 --> 01:29:46,100
Get out of my head (yells).

2256
01:29:46,100 --> 01:29:46,933
Mommy.

2257
01:29:48,100 --> 01:29:49,600
- How's Tom today?

2258
01:29:50,500 --> 01:29:52,833
(Tom yells)

2259
01:29:55,067 --> 01:29:56,533
- Help me, help me.

2260
01:29:56,533 --> 01:29:58,767
- We gotta read...

2261
01:29:58,767 --> 01:30:01,500
Ohp, we gotta read
a letter here?

2262
01:30:01,500 --> 01:30:03,533
Put this up on
Still Store, okay?

2263
01:30:03,533 --> 01:30:05,000
Put that up there.

2264
01:30:05,000 --> 01:30:06,867
Okay, that one, too.

2265
01:30:06,867 --> 01:30:11,033
And this is from Elden Crissy,
age seven, and they write,

2266
01:30:12,467 --> 01:30:15,033
Dear Joel, Crow, Tom,
Servo, and Gypsy,

2267
01:30:15,033 --> 01:30:16,567
I like your show a lot.

2268
01:30:16,567 --> 01:30:20,367
Whenever me and my dad watch
it, we can't stop laughing.

2269
01:30:20,367 --> 01:30:21,967
My favorite episode
was when a man

2270
01:30:21,967 --> 01:30:26,133
pointed to another man and
Crow yelled, "Pull my finger."

2271
01:30:28,733 --> 01:30:30,233
- What happened?

2272
01:30:30,233 --> 01:30:32,233
- Well, the thing tried to
jump me so I had to kill it.

2273
01:30:32,233 --> 01:30:33,367
Pretty much.

2274
01:30:33,367 --> 01:30:34,533
- Whaddya think, sirs?

2275
01:30:34,533 --> 01:30:35,833
- Did you see that?

2276
01:30:35,833 --> 01:30:39,600
He was using his
hand the whole time.

2277
01:30:39,600 --> 01:30:40,800
- Hi, TV's Frank.

2278
01:30:40,800 --> 01:30:42,133
My name is Fisty.

2279
01:30:42,133 --> 01:30:45,667
- Well if that don't
beat all (laughs).

2280
01:30:45,667 --> 01:30:47,600
How come they call ya Fisty?

2281
01:30:47,600 --> 01:30:49,933
- Here's why.
- That's Fisty.

2282
01:30:52,200 --> 01:30:54,367
(smack)

2283
01:30:54,367 --> 01:30:55,833
- Nice job, Fisty.

2284
01:30:55,833 --> 01:30:57,300
Push the button, will you?

2285
01:30:57,300 --> 01:30:58,633
- Live to serve.

2286
01:31:02,667 --> 01:31:06,167
(somber orchestral music)

2287
01:32:04,333 --> 01:32:06,567
(laughter)

